{"id": "35", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place on the baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, then bake in a preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place on the baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, then bake in a preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "time_sec": 8.316, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3434, 2291, 1261, 75252, 15241, 1454, 34262, 33578, 4681, 37173, 32308, 1044, 5526, 1278, 13396, 2017, 2339, 13886, 1454, 4962, 17970, 1321, 7244, 61170, 1044, 3535, 1408, 1278, 75252, 15241, 1321, 6240, 1454, 102398, 104