{"id": "37", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) (Passage 2).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper (Passage 1 and 2).\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet lined with butter-flavored cooking spray (Passage 1).\n4. Add onion, green pepper, and tomato slices to the baking sheet (Passage 1).\n5. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (Passage 1 and 2).\n6. To add cheesy flavor, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for an additional 3 minutes (Passage 3).\n\nNote that Passage 3 does not provide any specific instructions for cooking the pollock, but rather suggests adding cheese to the existing dish.", "pred": "Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place on the baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, then bake in a preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place on the baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, then bake in a preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Optionally, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, return the fish to the oven, and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "time_sec": 8.134, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remo