{"id": "42", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "pred": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. After that, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, dip a clean cloth in the solution, and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. After that, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, dip a clean cloth in the solution, and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "time_sec": 11.316, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 2012, 17985, 1848, 1307, 1261, 23702, 129544, 1044, 2158, 3160, 1278, 129544, 1408, 1261, 8385, 9436, 1394, 1032, 1050, 1048, 7334, 1317, 6444, 1262, 1278, 17985, 1046, 6830, 1044, 117910, 1278, 17985, 2490, 1454, 1261, 32656, 1505, 17985, 14260, 4427, 1505, 15504, 55941, 1569, 1044, 3144, 25052, 1605, 1317, 10605, 1278, 129544, 1681, 14772, 1046, 63882, 1032, 1049, 1317, 1032, 1050, 117433, 124538, 1307, 61122, 2223, 2140, 2357, 3245, 1317, 1261, 9375, 18473, 1321, 13523, 1278, 17985, 1317, 89736, 1494, 1046, 5417, 1455, 1044, 13523, 1278, 4457, 1454, 1261, 49922, 18473, 1317, 38124, 1415, 1278, 61122, 2223, 2140, 2357, 3245, 1046, 28978, 1032, 1049, 117433, 83372, 1307, 11301, 84603, 50584, 1454, 1032, 1049, 19339, 1307, 4180, 1044, 15018, 1261, 9375, 18473, 1294, 1278, 5097, 1044, 1321, 13523, 1278, 4457, 2790, 1046, 15513, 1044, 38124, 1415, 2903, 1454, 1261, 18473, 103387, 1294, 9375, 4180, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0858, -0.0347, -0.6395, -0.3262, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0197, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.0129, -1.0157, -0.0051, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0003, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.382, -0.4114, -0.0631, -0.0621, -0.0231, -0.0049, -0.0009, -1.0742, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0312, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0312, -0.5158, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.1565, -0.0, -0.0071, -0.0744, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1241, -0