{"id": "50", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "gt": "A water pick, also known as a Waterpik, is a beneficial tool for oral care. It is designed to shoot a strong stream of water at the gum line to help eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to get rid of with a toothbrush. It can also help maintain overall body health. In comparison to flossing, using a water pick can be easier and leave your mouth feeling cleaner. It can also massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis. It is especially useful in cleaning around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing cannot reach.", "pred": "Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue to reduce gingivitis risk, clean better around teeth and gums, and remove food from inaccessible areas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue to reduce gingivitis risk, clean better around teeth and gums, and remove food from inaccessible areas.", "time_sec": 5.125, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17231, 65438, 3508, 7766, 17580, 4612, 1536, 29521, 1261, 5666, 10197, 1307, 4180, 1513, 1278, 66282, 3110, 1317, 31924, 22146, 1115, 1321, 41345, 1044, 7702, 1294, 7224, 102394, 6560, 8132, 1046, 4159, 68664, 1321, 51578, 6444, 9392, 1317, 9980, 18616, 1354, 11505, 5735, 1044, 9375, 4942, 3879, 20277, 1321, 1343, 11558, 1044, 1321, 85