{"id": "53", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the benefits of using a water pick (also known as a Waterpik) include:\n\n1. Helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by eliminating germs and plaque.\n2. Being a great oral care tool for removing food from areas that brushing cannot access.\n3. Massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth to reduce the risk of gingivitis.\n4. Being an alternative to flossing and potentially offering similar benefits.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on other potential benefits of using a water pick, such as its ability to reach areas between teeth or its effectiveness in reducing plaque buildup.", "pred": "Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue to reduce gingivitis risk, clean better around teeth and gums, and remove food from inaccessible areas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue to reduce gingivitis risk, clean better around teeth and gums, and remove food from inaccessible areas.", "time_sec": 5.229, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17231, 65438, 3508, 7766, 17580, 4612, 1536, 29521, 1261, 5666, 10197, 1307, 4180, 1513, 1278, 66282, 3110, 1317, 31924, 22146, 1115, 1321, 41345, 1044, 7702, 1294, 7224, 102394, 6560, 8132, 1046, 4159, 68664, 1321, 