{"id": "77", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and continue cooking on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "pred": "To cook brats, first prick them with a fork to prevent exploding. Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Alternatively, after simmering, cook the bratwurst on a preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side. Cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for about 5 days or in the freezer for up to 3 months.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook brats, first prick them with a fork to prevent exploding. Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Alternatively, after simmering, cook the bratwurst on a preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side. Cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for about 5 days or in the freezer for up to 3 months.", "time_sec": 12.45, "nemotron": {"run