{"id": "78", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\nStep 1: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n\nStep 2: Lightly oil the grate.\n\nStep 3: Combine beer and onions in a large pot, bring to a boil, and submerge the bratwurst. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n\nStep 4: Simmer the bratwurst in the beer mixture for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n\nStep 5: Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and grill it on the preheated grill for an additional 5 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until browned and cooked through.\n\nStep 6: Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side dish.\n\nNote: It's important to prick the bratwurst with a fork before cooking to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Also, cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months.", "pred": "To cook brats, first prick them with a fork to prevent exploding. Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Alternatively, after simmering, cook the bratwurst on a preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side. Cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for about 5 days or in the freezer for up to 3 months.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook brats, first prick them with a fork to prevent exploding. Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat, lightly oil the grate, and cook the bratwurst for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Alternatively, after simmering, cook the bratwurst on a preheated grill for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side. Cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for about 5 days or in the freezer for up to 3 months.", "time_sec": 12.475, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 17966, 2795, 2476, 1044, 2158, 109485, 2424, 1454, 1261, 40191, 1317, 7495, 3543, 7967, 1046, 22435, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1294, 1261, 4329, 12169, 3418, 1454, 126255, 1044, 34262, 1044, 1321, 34568, 1046, 107178, 1317, 1261, 75766, 1044, 2430, 9980, 9374, 1317, 9566, 1321, 2500, 2221, 1394, 1032, 1049, 1053, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1048, 7334, 1046, 6438, 68155, 1420, 41730, 116260, 1394, 9566, 42709, 9374, 1044, 54199, 10673, 1278, 32090, 1044, 1321, 17966, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1394, 1032, 1049, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1052, 7334, 1044, 19826, 32082, 1317, 22980, 66670, 1046, 37346, 1044, 2453, 2500, 2221, 1302, 1044, 17966, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1408, 1261, 1750, 1268, 1621, 116260, 1394, 1032, 1053, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1048, 7334, 1044, 19826, 5785, 1046, 4579, 1672, 1454, 1278, 34568, 13810, 1435, 1261, 1317, 13633, 1505, 4258, 1046, 22141, 1286, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1710, 1402, 11489, 1294, 1278, 101671, 1394, 2314, 1032, 1053, 5072, 1505, 1294, 1278, 5370, 5176, 1394, 2015, 1317, 1032, 1051, 6972, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0962, -0.0962, -0.3934, -0.0004, -0.4592, -0.0003, -0.013, -0.7068, -0.0943, -0.1437, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0424, -0.0003, -0.5804, 0.0, -0.4838, -0.8269, -0.8728, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.3394, -0.0, -0.5405, -0.084, -0.0162, -0.0003, -0.0017, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0035, -0.0001, -0.3998, -0.7068, -0.6155, -0.0001, -0.0127, -0.1158, -0.0296, -