{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "The body systems work together in several ways. The urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, including the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs. For example, the skeletal system works with the muscular system to enable movement, while the circulatory system transports nutrients and oxygen to the body's cells and removes waste products. The digestive system breaks down food and absorbs nutrients, which are then transported by the circulatory system to the body's cells. The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, and the nervous system controls and coordinates all other systems.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The body systems work together in several ways. The urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, including the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs. For example, the skeletal system works with the muscular system to enable movement, while the circulatory system transports nutrients and oxygen to the body's cells and removes waste products. The digestive system breaks down food and absorbs nutrients, which are then transported by the circulatory system to the body's cells. The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, and the nervous system controls and coordinates all other systems.", "time_sec": 12.957, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 4212, 6467, 2196, 5823, 1294, 4631, 9384, 1046, 1531, 42656, 2663, 3689, 1545, 18052, 8066, 1562, 1278, 45014, 1044, 51403, 1044, 88136, 1044, 23730, 1044, 4087, 33012, 1044, 1321, 25199, 6467, 1044, 3907, 1278, 80323, 1321, 4953, 46527, 2783, 1046, 1531, 23730, 2663, 8222, 14297, 1394, 1747, 4212, 8262, 1321, 53934, 10006, 42812, 1562, 1278, 51403, 1044, 88136, 1044, 45014, 1044, 4087, 33012, 1044, 42656, 1044, 1321, 25199, 6467, 1044, 3907, 1278, 24917, 1044, 1295, 105081, 1044, 75396, 1097, 1044, 1321, 40707, 1046, 2898, 3336, 1044, 1278, 45014, 2663, 6113, 1454, 1278, 51403, 2663, 1317, 14975, 9014, 1044, 3016, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 49489, 48824, 1321, 14297, 1317, 1278, 4212, 1681, 3459, 1321, 53934, 18052, 8066, 1046, 1531, 88136, 2663, 31322, 3151, 6939, 1321, 24127, 5136, 48824, 1044, 1799, 1584, 2430, 45947, 1536, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 1317, 1278, 4212, 1681, 345