{"id": "106", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "pred": "The body systems work together in several ways. The urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, including the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs. For example, the skeletal system works with the muscular system to enable movement, while the circulatory system transports nutrients and oxygen to the body's cells and removes waste products. The digestive system breaks down food and absorbs nutrients, which are then transported by the circulatory system to the body's cells. The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, and the nervous system controls and coordinates all other systems.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The body systems work together in several ways. The urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, including the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs. For example, the skeletal system works with the muscular system to enable movement, while the circulatory system transports nutrients and oxygen to the body's cells and removes waste products. The digestive system breaks down food and absorbs nutrients, which are then transported by the circulatory system to the body's cells. The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, and the nervous system controls and coordinates all other systems.", "time_sec": 13.17, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 4212, 6467, 2196, 5823, 1294, 4631, 9384, 1046, 1531, 42656, 2663, 3689, 1545, 18052, 8066, 1562, 1278, 45014, 1044, 51403, 1044, 88136, 1044, 23730, 1044, 4087, 33012, 1044, 1321, 25199, 6467, 1044, 3907, 1278, 80323, 1321, 4953, 46527, 2783, 1046, 1531, 23730, 2663, 8222, 14297, 1394, 1747, 4212, 8262, 1321, 53934, 10006, 42812, 1562, 1278, 51403, 1044, 88136, 1044, 45014, 1044, 4087, 33012, 1044, 42656, 1044, 1321, 25199, 6467, 1044, 3907, 1278, 24917, 1044, 1295, 105081, 1044, 75396, 1097, 1044, 1321, 40707, 1046, 2898, 3336, 1044, 1278, 45014, 2663, 6113, 1454, 1278, 51403, 2663, 1317, 14975, 9014, 1044, 3016, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 49489, 48824, 1321, 14297, 1317, 1278, 4212, 1681, 3459, 1321, 53934, 18052, 8066, 1046, 1531, 88136, 2663, 31322, 3151, 6939, 1321, 24127, 5136, 48824, 1044, 1799, 1584, 2430, 45947, 1536, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 1317, 1278, 4212, 1681, 3459, 1046, 1531, 80583, 2663, 22444, 52832, 1455, 32360, 5561, 74456, 7389, 1044, 3907, 6762, 1321, 4900, 1044, 1321, 1278, 25199, 2663, 12559, 1321, 21939, 1747, 2147, 6467, 1046, 11], "logp_