{"id": "113", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of it. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. After these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner. If the original certificate is lost, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of it, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. An additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed, notarized, and is furnished by the Company.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of it, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. An additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed, notarized, and is furnished by the Company.", "time_sec": 6.624, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17231, 29443, 1584, 17845, 1536, 19566, 1278, 14451, 17231, 18196, 75923, 1044, 37692, 1278, 2595, 1307, 1494, 1044, 11495, 17686, 1307, 30269, 1536, 1278, 1875, 16692, 1044, 1321, 33235, 1261, 1659, 1055, 1053, 1046, 1048, 1048, 32068, 1317, 2832, 1278, 690