{"id": "115", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, water shares can be transferred through the issuance of a new Water Stock Certificate to the new owner of record after paying a fee of $75.00. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner must provide proof of ownership before a transfer can be processed. Additionally, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of it, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. An additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed, notarized, and is furnished by the Company.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of it, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. An additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed, notarized, and is furnished by the Company.", "time_sec": 6.79, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17231, 29443, 1584, 17845, 1536, 19566, 1278, 14451, 17231, 18196, 75923, 1044, 37692, 1278, 2595, 1307, 1494, 1044, 11495, 17686, 1307, 30269, 1536, 1278, 1875, 16692, 1044, 1321, 33235, 1261, 1659, 1055, 1053, 1046, 1048, 1048, 32068, 1317, 2832, 1278, 6904, 1046, 2048