{"id": "118", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares includes the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, if necessary.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how water shares are transferred is: By following the steps outlined above, which include the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying the required fees.", "pred": "Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of it, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. An additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed, notarized, and is furnished by the Company.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water shares are transferred by returning the assigned Water Stock Certificate, signing the back of it, providing proof of ownership by the new owner, and paying a $75.00 fee to process the transfer. An additional $75.00 fee is required when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, and the document must be signed, notarized, and is furnished by the Company.", "time_sec": 6.419, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 311