{"id": "120", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "pred": "The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and is associated with \"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'\" in Spanish, with an etymology linked to the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and is associated with \"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'\" in Spanish, with an etymology linked to the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "time_sec": 6.745, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 2564, 45038, 4938, 1429, 2596, 1466, 1034, 1294, 18626, 1044, 1429, 41302, 1118, 5683, 1034, 1294, 16506, 1044, 1321, 1395, 4963, 1454, 1429, 2266, 1307, 2295, 7676, 90336, 1576, 37775, 12530, 1307, 9554, 5691, 1039, 1321, 1576, 52881, 1983, 1307, 23500, 10621, 38416, 1294, 16382, 1044, 1454, 1420, 1568, 2360, 3678, 14078, 1317, 1278, 18626, 1429, 1781, 2033, 1259, 1034, 10138, 1429, 1611, 26932, 1044, 5999, 1118, 5683, 1034, 1505, 1429, 1781, 1346, 1034, 10138, 1429, 484