{"id": "123", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the meaning of the name Teresa is:\n\n* Reap; from Therasia (Greek)\n* Reaper; from Therasia (American)\n* Harvester (Italian)\n* Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux' (Spanish)\n\nIt is also mentioned that the name Teresa is a Greek baby name, an American baby name, an Italian baby name, and a Spanish baby name.\n\nTherefore, the meaning of the name Teresa can vary depending on the culture and language, but it generally means \"reaper\" or \"harvester\", and is also associated with the names of two popular saints.", "pred": "The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and is associated with \"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'\" in Spanish, with an etymology linked to the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The name Teresa means \"Reap\" in Greek, \"Harvester\" in Italian, and is associated with \"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'\" in Spanish, with an etymology linked to the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "time_sec": 6.894, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 2564, 45038, 4938, 1429, 2596, 1466, 1034, 1294, 18626, 1044, 1429, 41302, 1118, 5683, 1034, 1294, 16506, 1044, 1321, 1395, 4963, 1454, 1429, 2266, 1307, 2295, 7676, 90336, 1576, 37775, 12530, 1307, 9554, 5691, 1039, 1321, 1576, 52881, 1983, 1307, 23500, 10621, 38416, 1294, 16382, 1044, 1454, 1420, 1568, 2360, 3678, 14078, 1317, 1278, 18626, 1429, 1781,