{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.686, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 71297, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1881, -0.0326, -0.9381, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0007], "cumulative_logprob": -1.1599, "norm_logp": -0.0967, "input_len": 443, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "127", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Sure! Here's my attempt to answer your question based on the provided passages:\n\nHow do you prepare the site for building a lean-to shed?\n\nAccording to passage 1, step 1, you should prepare the site by laying down a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. This will provide a stable base for the shed's foundation. Additionally, passage 2 mentions cutting two pressure-treated 4x4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids, which will serve as the foundation for the shed. Finally, passage 3 provides instructions for building the shed's floor, including cutting rim joists to a length of 6 feet. Based on these passages, it appears that preparing the site involves laying down a layer of gravel and setting the skids in place before constructing the floor.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.696, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 71297, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1881, -0.0326, -0.9381, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0007], "cumulative_logprob": -1.1599, "norm_logp": -0.0967, "input_len": 443, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.59, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
