{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "As per the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: As per the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.", "time_sec": 4.9, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 2813, 1651, 1278, 90818, 32243, 5845, 1044, 2200, 1420, 24596, 1395, 57045, 1536, 1278, 6170, 1809, 1605, 6981, 1044, 6079, 1032, 1052, 1051, 1040, 1054, 1041, 45632, 1278, 42739, 2632, 1307, 1278, 24596, 1317, 1402, 7896, 1562, 1278, 4950, 1294, 1278, 4607, 2637, 1294, 1799, 1278, 24596, 1395, 57045, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.088, -0.0021, -0.5167, -0.0, -0.5362, -0.0082, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0357, -0.0369, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0115, -0.4815, -0.0, -0.1089, -0.0095, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.181, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0, 0