{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "As per the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: As per the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.", "time_sec": 4.511, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 2813, 1651, 1278, 90818, 32243, 5845, 1044, 2200, 1420, 24596, 1395, 57045, 1536, 1278, 6170, 1809, 1605, 6981, 1044, 6079, 1032, 1052, 1051, 1040, 1054, 1041, 45632, 1278, 42739, 2632, 1307, 1278, 24596, 1317, 1402, 7896, 1562, 1278, 4950, 1294, 1278, 4607, 2637, 1294, 1799, 1278, 24596, 1395, 57045, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.088, -0.0021, -0.5167, -0.0, -0.5362, -0.0082, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0357, -0.0369, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0115, -0.4815, -0.0, -0.1089, -0.0095, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.181, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.