{"id": "173", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to soften sugar:\n\n1. To soften brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days. (Passage 1)\n2. To soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200°F), remove the sugar from its package, and place it in an ovenproof container. Warm the sugar in the oven for about 15 minutes, then tap it with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, leave it in the oven for a longer period of time to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. To keep brown sugar soft, pack it into the smallest container possible to minimize air exposure. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to soften other types of sugar, such as confectioner's sugar.", "pred": "To soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it for approximately 15 minutes. If the sugar begins to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave it inside for an hour or two to dry completely. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container to prevent hardening. For brown sugar, keep it sealed in an airtight container with minimal air exposure, using a small container to limit air space between the sugar and the lid, and place a damp paper towel or napkin on top of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, covering tightly; remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it for approximately 15 minutes. If the sugar begins to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave it inside for an hour or two to dry completely. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container to prevent hardening. For brown sugar, keep it sealed in an airtight container with minimal air exposure, using a small container to limit air space between the sugar and the lid, and place a damp paper towel or napkin on top of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, covering tightly; remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days.", "time_sec": 11.585, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 6444, 1262, 100152, 7272, 6557, 24224, 1044, 1750, 68155, 1278, 47139, 1317, 1278, 20755, 6138, 1319, 1049, 1053, 1048, 1045, 1050, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1574, 3535, 1278, 24224, 1294, 1420, 47139, 65708, 11024, 1044, 1321, 15701, 1494, 1394, 11267, 1032, 1049, 1053, 7334, 1046, 3367, 1278, 24224, 19570, 1317, 6962, 13292, 1044, 3884, 2490, 1278, 47139, 1321, 9288, 1494, 6625, 1394, 1420, 12271, 1505, 2295, 1317, 12689, 10185, 1046, 53119, 8141, 7272, 6557, 24224, 1294, 1420, 4864, 1116, 1620, 11024, 1317, 7495, 118152, 1046, 2898, 22980, 24224, 1044, 5807, 1494, 38138, 1294, 1420, 4864, 1116, 1620, 11024, 1454, 19629, 4864, 11915, 1044, 2505, 1261, 3709, 11024, 1317, 6139, 4864, 5702, 2396, 1278, 24224, 1321, 1278, 20033, 1044, 1321, 3535, 1261, 49922, 7873, 74537, 1505, 11261, 7533, 1408, 3977, 1307, 17985, 30711, 1505, 69054, 2136, 1278, 24224, 1044, 24879, 40363, 1059, 8559, 1278, 49922, 7873, 74537, 2453, 1261, 8580, 1307, 5072, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1851, -0.0115, -0.3758, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0956, -0.1005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0383, -0.0193, -0.0, -0.2091, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1381, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0054, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0014, -0.0025, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.