{"id": "179", "question": "how to change the sleep time on my computer", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to change the sleep time on my computer\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click the Start menu and select Control Panel.\n2. In the Control Panel, click on Power Options.\n3. In the Power Options window, click on \"Change when the computer sleeps\" on the left side of the window.\n4. In the \"Put the computer to sleep\" section, change the duration of time to the desired amount of time you want the computer to sit idle before it goes to sleep.\n5. Alternatively, you can also toggle off the option to enter Sleep mode automatically.\n\nIf you are using Windows 10, you can also search for \"Power Options\" in the taskbar search box and select it to open the Power Options window.\n\nIf you are using Windows 8.1 / Windows RT 8.1, you can move your mouse to the lower left-hand corner of the screen, right-click the Start button, and select Shut down or sign out, and then select Shut down.", "pred": "To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps based on the provided passages:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps based on the provided passages:  \n\n1. **For Windows 7**:  \n   - Click the Start Menu, select Control Panel, then choose \"Power Management Settings\" in the search field.  \n   - Click \"Change Power Management settings,\" then on the left side of the Power Options window, select \"Change when the computer sleeps.\"  \n   - Adjust the \"Put the computer to sleep\" entry to your desired idle time (e.g., 10 minutes, 30 minutes) or disable sleep mode entirely.  \n\n2. **For Windows 10**:  \n   - Click the Start Menu, type \"power options\" in the taskbar search box, and select \"Power Options.\"  \n   - From there, adjust the sleep settings (though the passage does not specify the exact steps for modifying the sleep time, it directs you to the Power Options menu).  \n\nThe passages do not provide steps for Windows 8.1/RT 8.1 sleep time adjustments, so the above applies to Windows 7 and 10.  \n\nAnswer: To change the sleep time on your computer, for Windows 7: Click", "time_sec": 18.499, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 4036, 1278, 10301, 2142, 1408, 2143, 8648, 1044, 2685, 2576, 9578, 4057, 1408, 1278, 5662, 42679, 1058, 1256, 1267, 1049, 1046, 1603, 4393, 10986, 1032, 1055, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1256, 1462, 30476, 1278, 13336, 28517, 1044, 5762, 15296, 48186, 1044, 2430, 12729, 1429, 29453, 18208, 36831, 1034, 1294, 1278, 6123, 3727, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1256, 1462, 30476, 1429, 8241, 14254, 18208, 11846, 4225, 2430, 1408, 1278, 3979, 4258, 1307, 1278, 14254, 47191, 7404, 1044, 5762, 1429, 8241, 2200, 1278, 8648, 16450, 22208, 2613, 1256, 1010, 1256, 1462, 80239, 1278, 1429, 38742, 1278, 8648, 1317, 10301, 1034, 10505, 1317, 2143, 14024, 59095, 2142, 1319, 1101, 3596, 3109, 1032, 1049, 1048, 7334, 1044, 1032, 1051, 1048, 7334, 1041, 1505, 28653, 10301, 7172, 17262, 1046, 1256, 1267, 1050, 1046, 1603, 4393, 10986, 1032, 1049, 1048, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1256, 1462, 30476, 1278, 13336, 28517, 1044, 2658, 1429, 33607, 7791, 1034, 1294, 1278, 6255, 3947, 6123, 7616, 1044, 1321, 5762, 1429, 29453, 47191, 2613, 1256, 1010, 1256, 1462, 8956, 2156, 1044, 9447, 1278, 10301, 11846, 1319, 4562, 1278, 14456, 3120, 1605, 22077, 1278, 7092, 9578, 1394, 51106, 1278, 10301, 2142, 1044, 1494, 95529, 1636, 1317, 1278, 14254, 47191, 12804, 1577, 1256, 1267, 1784, 42679, 1653, 1605, 5234, 9578, 1394, 10986, 1032, 1056, 1046, 1049, 1047, 19891, 1032, 1056, 1046, 1049, 10301, 21