{"id": "180", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "pred": "Psychological hugs, as described in the passages, are achieved through the use of empathy and listening skills (empathic listening), which can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. These skills may make a conversation partner feel as though they are receiving a hug, providing psychological comfort.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Psychological hugs, as described in the passages, are achieved through the use of empathy and listening skills (empathic listening), which can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. These skills may make a conversation partner feel as though they are receiving a hug, providing psychological comfort.", "time_sec": 5.201, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 113489, 39638, 1115, 1044, 1435, 5055, 1294, 1278, 42679, 1044, 1584, 12955, 2645, 1278, 2210, 1307, 84329, 1321, 27575, 14627, 1319, 5636, 1682, 1290, 27575, 1574, 1799, 1710, 3820, 1317, 3683, 14608, 1044, 20120, 104720, 1044, 1321, 15015, 80183, 1046, 4634, 14627, 2188, 3180, 1261, 18106, 