{"id": "182", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the physiological effects of hugging are numerous and significant. Hugs affect the entire body and can potentially be compared to the effects of multiple drugs operating at once. Furthermore, the act of hugging can also have psychological effects. Empathic listening can lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships, as well as making conversation partners feel like they are receiving a hug, which can provide comfort and ease their existential fears. Overall, the psychological effects of hugging are positive and suggest that this simple gesture can have a significant impact on our emotional and physical wellbeing.", "pred": "Psychological hugs, as described in the passages, are achieved through the use of empathy and listening skills (empathic listening), which can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. These skills may make a conversation partner feel as though they are receiving a hug, providing psychological comfort.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Psychological hugs, as described in the passages, are achieved through the use of empathy and listening skills (empathic listening), which can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. These skills may make a conversation partner feel as though they are receiving a hug, providing psychological comfort.", "time_sec": 5.231, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 113489, 39638, 1115, 1044, 1435, 5055, 1294, 1278, 42679, 1044, 1584, 12955, 2645, 1278, 2210, 1307, 84329, 1321, 27575, 14627, 1319, 5636, 1682, 1290, 27575, 1574, 1799, 1710, 3820, 1317, 