{"id": "194", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding (Passage 1).\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect (Passage 1).\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, making sure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame (Passage 1).\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames (Passage 1).\n5. Test ideas by laying the group of multiple pictures out on the floor first (Passage 2).\n6. Screw the frame to the backer board, repeat with each frame, and attach a hanging wire to the back (Passage 3).\n\nIt's important to note that the passages do not provide specific information on how to attach multiple frames together other than the steps mentioned above. Therefore, if more detailed instructions are needed, it may be best to consult additional resources or seek advice from a professional framer.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement at the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement at the same distance from 