{"id": "210", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 4.621, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 68175, 1584, 13173, 31580, 16815, 1307, 2342, 1925, 2658, 1307, 20293, 1046, 6860, 5961, 1584, 13173, 31580, 3214, 1307, 2295, 1505, 2081, 2801, 6689, 75991, 63290, 5823, 1046, 13064, 29