{"id": "211", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded, allowing for easy separation of the components using physical methods.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 4.762, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 68175, 1584, 13173, 31580, 16815, 1307, 2342, 1925, 2658, 1307, 20293, 1046, 6860, 5961, 1584, 13173, 31580, 3214, 1307, 2295, 1505, 2081, 2801, 6689, 75991, 63290, 5823, 1046, 13064, 29059, 1584, 8137, 25674, 1307, 6689, 1505, 13136, 2478, 1278, 7995, 1584, 1605, 75991, 63290, 1321, 1710, 1402, 17205, 1536, 8137, 4938, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1103, -0.0436, -0.1699, -0.0043, -0.2723, -0.0137, -0.5485, -0.0004, -0.342, -0