{"id": "212", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 4.633, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 68175, 1584, 13173, 31580, 16815, 1307, 2342, 1925, 2658, 1307, 20293, 1046, 6860, 5961, 1584, 13173, 31580, 3214, 1307, 2295, 1505, 2081, 2801, 6689, 75991, 63290, 5823, 1046, 13064, 29059, 1584, 8137, 25674, 1307, 6689, 1505, 13136, 2478, 1278, 7995, 1584, 1605, 75991, 63290, 1321, 1710, 1402, 17205, 1536, 8137, 4938, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1103, -0.0436, -0.1699, -0.0043, -0.2723, -0.0137, -0.5485, -0.0004, -0.342, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.5625, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0167, -0.0, -0.2858, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0793, -0.0006, -0.0898, -0.001, -0.0587, -0.024, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0364, -0.0012, -0.4731, -0.2827, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3559, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0341, -0.1427, -0.0, -0.1427, -0.5657, -0.4214], "cumulative_logprob": -5.0902, "norm_logp": -0.0909, "input_len": 475, "output_tokens": 56, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.93, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "213", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are:\n\n* Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. They have a fixed composition and cannot be broken down into simpler substances by physical means.\n* Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. They have a fixed composition and are pure substances.\n* Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. They have a variable composition and can be separated by physical means.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are their composition, bonding, and separability. Elements are homogeneous and have a fixed composition, compounds are heterogeneous and have a fixed composition, and mixtures are heterogeneous and have a variable composition. Additionally, elements and compounds are chemically bonded, while mixtures are not.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 4.676, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 68175, 1584, 13173, 31580, 16815, 1307, 2342, 1925, 2658, 1307, 20293, 1046, 6860, 5961, 1584, 13173, 31580, 3214, 1307, 2295, 1505, 2081, 2801, 6689, 75991, 63290, 5823, 1046, 13064, 29059, 1584, 8137, 25674, 1307, 6689, 1505, 13136, 2478, 1278, 7995, 1584, 1605, 75991, 63290, 1321, 1710, 1402, 17205, 1536, 8137, 4938, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1103, -0.0436, -0.1699, -0.0043, -0.2723, -0.0137, -0.5485, -0.0004, -0.342, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.5625, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0167, -0.0, -0.2858, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0793, -0.0006, -0.0898, -0.001, -0.0587, -0.024, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0364, -0.0012, -0.4731, -0.2827, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3559, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0341, -0.1427, -0.0, -0.1427, -0.5657, -0.4214], "cumulative_logprob": -5.0902, "norm_logp": -0.0909, "input_len": 475, "output_tokens": 56, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.97, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—on the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour‑sack towel.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—on the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour‑sack towel.", "time_sec": 10.378, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 35668, 23592, 43877, 17103, 1044, 2158, 9215, 1261, 74537, 1294, 1278, 24758, 3066, 31073, 1494, 1454, 8480, 4180, 1046, 90558, 1925, 11035, 1513, 1261, 2142, 1317, 10035, 10605, 1044, 2989, 1332, 4604, 1278, 39922, 1294, 1925, 2786, 1046, 13516, 1261, 3709, 5647, 1307, 23852, 105396, 2342, 2478, 6618, 1674, 1263, 1278, 9478, 1321, 3879, 1278, 17211, 88784, 7495, 50584, 1562, 33578, 8045, 2143, 4275, 11035, 1307, 23592, 1046, 2898, 83976, 23592, 31645, 1044, 89736, 1261, 3709, 5647, 1307, 75252, 89703, 1294, 8480, 4180, 1044, 2878, 1494, 3679, 1294, 1278, 11035, 1394, 1261, 4517, 7334, 1044, 1321, 3894, 1278, 89703, 1317, 89736, 1278, 31645, 1046, 5417, 72727, 1302, 43850, 1454, 8480, 4180, 1044, 12689, 1278, 43877, 1454, 1261, 17208, 91012, 109431, 37434, 18473, 2516, 1435, 6188, 1102, 6144, 1505, 1261, 36590, 109431, 1115, 1663, 74537, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0263, -0.0153, -0.1359, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0621, -0.8848, -0.0564, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.696, -0.0004, -0.3942, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4285, -0.0088, -0.0017, -0.5719, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1636, -0.0502, -0.004, -0.5761, -0.5141, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.3917, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.5202, -0.0036, -0.0297, -0.0058, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0889, -0.0001, -0.1498, -0.2871, -0.0009, -0.4451, -0.78, -0.0, -0.0034, -0.1985, -0.1249, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5276, -0.008, -0.0095, -0.2524, -0.6319, -0.0, -0.8397, -0.0303, -0.282