{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—on the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour‑sack towel.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—on the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a s