{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—on the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour‑sack towel.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, cradling the bowl in one hand. Use a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—on the bottom and around the rim—to prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and allow the soda to dissolve the residue. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the glasses with a smooth lint‑free cloth such as microfiber or a flour‑sack towel.", "time_sec": 10.42, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 35668, 23592, 43877, 17103, 1044, 2158, 9215, 1261, 74537, 1294, 1278, 24758, 3066, 31073, 1494, 1454, 8480, 4180, 1046, 90558, 1925, 11035, 1513, 1261, 2142, 1317, 10035, 10605, 1044, 2989, 1332, 4604, 1278, 39922, 1294, 1925, 2786, 1046, 13516, 1261, 3709, 5647, 1307, 23852, 105396, 2342, 2478, 6618, 1674, 1263, 1278, 9478, 1321, 3879, 1278, 17211, 88784, 7495, 50584, 1562, 33578, 8045, 2143, 4275, 11035, 1307, 23592, 1046, 2898, 83976, 23592, 31645, 1044, 89736, 1261, 3709, 5647, 1307, 75252, 89703, 1294, 8480, 4180, 1044, 2878, 1494, 3679, 1294, 1278, 11035, 1394, 1261, 4517, 7334, 1044, 1321, 3894, 1278, 89703, 1317, 89736, 1278, 31645, 1046, 5417, 72727, 1302, 43850, 1454, 8480, 4180, 1044, 12689, 1278, 43877, 1454, 1261, 17208, 91012, 109431, 37434, 18473, 2516, 1435, 6188, 1102, 6144, 1505, 1261, 36590, 109431, 1115, 1663, 74537, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0263, -0.0153, -0.1359, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0621, -0.8848, -0.0564, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.696, -0.0004, -0.3942, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4285, -0.0088, -0.0017, -0.5719, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1636, -0.0502, -0.004, -0.5761, -0.5141, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.3917, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.5202, -0.0036, -0.0297, -0.0058, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0889, -0.0001, -0.1498, -0.2871, -0.0009, -0.4451, -0.78, -0.0, -0.0034, -0.1985, -0.1249, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5276, -0.008, -0.0095, -0.2524, -0.6319, -0.0, -0.8397, -0.0303, -0.282, -0.1607, -0.0, -0.0113, -0.9881, -0.0047, -0.0124, -0.0007, -0.0146, -0.0348, -0.1554, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.2549, -0.0001, -0.0,