{"id": "231", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "pred": "Oil stains on a concrete driveway can be removed using several methods. These include using oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as compared in a video. For fresh or small stubborn stains, the poultice method is recommended. Before cleaning, wash off dirt and debris with water from a hose or bucket, avoiding high pressure to prevent pushing oil deeper. Commercial-grade cleaners can be applied, scrubbed with a brush or broom, and then cleaned with a pressure washer using detergent, ensuring even spraying and consistent nozzle distance to avoid streaking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Oil stains on a concrete driveway can be removed using several methods. These include using oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, or carburetor cleaner, as compared in a video. For fresh or small stubborn stains, the poultice method is recommended. Before cleaning, wash off dirt and debris with water from a hose or bucket, avoiding high pressure to prevent pushing oil deeper. Commercial-grade cleaners can be applied, scrubbed with a brush or broom, and then cleaned with a pressure washer using detergent, ensuring even spraying and consistent nozzle distance to avoid streaking.", "time_sec": 9.059, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 35663, 117387, 1408, 1261, 21165, 92584, 1710, 1402, 9905, 2505, 4631, 6021, 1046, 4634, 4626, 2505, 47139, 64211, 1044, 1974, 1484, 2786, 64211, 1044, 1505, 28024, 1549, 20468, 64211, 1044, 1435, 5496, 1294, 1261, 7476, 1046, 2898, 14420, 1505, 3709, 83976, 117387, 1044, 1278, 6212, 3234, 1702, 2866, 1395, 17201, 1046, 20218, 28685, 1044, 35668, 2490, 47945, 1321, 50629, 1454, 4180, 1562, 1261, 94540, 1505, 37688, 1044, 40052, 2738, 6909, 1317, 7495, 34100, 10673, 29348, 1046, 54136, 53354, 9375, 1428, 1710, 1402, 7960, 1044, 74570, 3507, 1454, 1261, 31779, 1505, 4163, 1313, 1044, 1321, 2430, 49407, 1454, 1261, 6909, 1486, 1900, 2505, 105396, 1044, 40227, 3199, 114072, 1321, 12714, 48727, 7786, 1317, 10035, 12614, 6812, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1602, -0.0051, -0.4347, -0.0011, -0.0077, -0.2805, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0245, -0.0005, -0.0428, -0.0072, -0.8584, -0.001, -0.6762, -1.2705, -0.0103, -0.2896, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.5934, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.2631, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.2578, -0.0192, -0.064, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0001, -0.0416, -0.5504, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0019, -0.2502, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1065, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3182, -0.0005, -0.0269, -0.278, -0.2027, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.4375, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0216, -0.0001, -0.0075, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0171, -0.3895, -0.037, -0.2866, -0.0674, -0.0, -0.0137, -0.053, -0.0, -0.4111, -0.7132, -0.0027, -0.0014,