{"id": "233", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.627, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 71297, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0947, -0.0156, -0.5, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0016], "cumulative_logprob": -0.6123, "norm_logp": -0.051, "input_len": 501, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "235", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.622, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 71297, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0947, -0.0156, -0.5, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0016], "cumulative_logprob": -0.6123, "norm_logp": -0.051, "input_len": 501, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "236", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.683, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 71297, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0947, -0.0156, -0.5, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0016], "cumulative_logprob": -0.6123, "norm_logp": -0.051, "input_len": 501, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.1, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "240", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The trap is designed as a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance, and crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food inside. The design allows crabs to enter but not exit.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The trap is designed as a large square, about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with two ends featuring lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance, and crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food inside. The design allows crabs to enter but not exit.", "time_sec": 8.39, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 1067, 5988, 76686, 2196, 1536, 2505, 1261, 2663, 1307, 94845, 6625, 1261, 4329, 8893, 4