{"id": "245", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does.", "pred": "One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA only requires that a disability limits a major life activity, without the \"substantial\" requirement.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: One key difference is that the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a substantial limitation of a major life activity, whereas the FEHA only requires that a disability limits a major life activity, without the \"substantial\" requirement.", "time_sec": 6.991, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 5661, 3844, 6592, 1395, 1455, 1278, 10195, 1065, 28735, 1317, 3167, 14670, 53032, 1454, 3946, 1317, 37209, 17942, 1321, 104125, 2396, 3167, 1321, 2065, 53032, 1044, 3016, 1278, 48414, 23303, 28735, 1317, 2081, 17942, 1321, 3120, 1605, 24924, 2396, 3167, 1321, 2065, 53032, 1046, 18011, 1044, 2425, 1278, 10195, 1065, 1044