{"id": "256", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "pred": "To clean your dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct isn't fastened, it should slide out easily. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole. Then, go to the back of the dryer, unscrew the vent clamp, and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning, which can improve dryer efficiency.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean your dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct isn't fastened, it should slide out easily. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole. Then, go to the back of the dryer, unscrew the vent clamp, and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning, which can improve dryer efficiency.", "time_sec": 10.682, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-c