{"id": "257", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "pred": "To clean your dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct isn't fastened, it should slide out easily. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole. Then, go to the back of the dryer, unscrew the vent clamp, and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning, which can improve dryer efficiency.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean your dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it. If the vent duct isn't fastened, it should slide out easily. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole. Then, go to the back of the dryer, unscrew the vent clamp, and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Clean lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the brush. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean around the lint filter area for more thorough cleaning, which can improve dryer efficiency.", "time_sec": 10.707, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 9375, 2143, 129544, 8117, 1044, 2158, 42668, 1278, 129544, 8117, 6432, 1408, 1278, 7805, 1307, 2143, 5718, 1321, 8559, 1494, 1046, 3367, 1278, 8117, 32957, 10045, 2405, 113482, 1044, 1494, 2715, 25709, 1848, 10421, 1046, 13516, 1261, 129544, 8117, 31779, 1317, 8559, 91012, 1562, 6625, 1278, 18441, 1046, 6830, 1044, 1974, 1317, 1278, 2595, 1307, 1278, 129544, 1044, 7447, 101773, 1278, 8117, 62157, 1044, 1321, 25709, 1278, 8117, 1848, 1307, 1278, 55859, 26144, 12201, 1046, 42271, 91012, 1562, 2960, 1278, 8117, 1321, 1278, 18441, 1294, 1278, 2595, 1307, 1278, 129544, 2505, 1278, 31779, 1046, 1871, 16762, 1278, 8117, 1321, 6920, 1278, 129544, 2595, 3675, 1278, 8751, 1046, 18011, 1044, 1636, 2188, 2933, 1317, 8559, 1278, 9478, 5346, 12321, 1307, 1278, 129544, 1321, 9375, 3879, 1278, 91012, 7367, 4457, 1394, 2081, 27342, 28685, 1044, 1799, 1710, 10591, 129544, 13873, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0275, -0.0653, -0.1651, -0.0001, -1.049, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0046, -0.6651, -0.0639, -0.2662, -0.2735, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0108, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.0, -0.0053, -0.0002, -0.1811, -0.0001, -0.0151, -0.7628, -0