{"id": "271", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "gt": "The earliest signs of pregnancy often include mood swings and unusual emotional behavior due to a flood of hormones in the body. Dizziness can also occur as pregnancy causes blood vessels to dilate and blood pressure to drop. Other early symptoms can include a missed period, bloating, spotting, and cramping. Approximately half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, and around 3 in 10 women experience nausea without vomiting, with these symptoms typically starting around six weeks after their last period.", "pred": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy mentioned in the passages include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea, and vomiting. Mood swings are due to hormonal changes in early pregnancy, dizziness results from blood vessel dilation and lowered blood pressure, while bloating, spotting, and cramping are other early indicators that can be easily overlooked. Nausea and vomiting, affecting around half of all pregnant women, typically start around six weeks after the last period.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy mentioned in the passages include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea, and vomiting. Mood swings are due to hormonal changes in early pregnancy, dizziness results from blood vessel dilation and lowered blood pressure, while bloating, spotting, and cramping are other early indicators that can be easily overlooked. Nausea and vomiting, affecting around half of all pregnant women, typically start around six weeks after the last period.", "time_sec": 8.122, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_i