IE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "294", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "To properly fertilize your grass, you should fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for your specific grass type. For warm season grasses, this would be when the grass turns green in the early spring. You should also know the type of fertilizer to use based on the type of grass you have and do a pH soil test to ensure the fertilizer has the appropriate pH for your soil. Once you've determined the correct fertilizer and timing, apply it in a perpendicular pattern and check the lawn after application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape, but if it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "pred": "Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season, specifically when warm season grasses begin to turn green in spring, after determining the appropriate fertilizer type based on your grass type and conducting a pH soil test, and apply the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern while ensuring the lawn is not over-fertilized by checking if the leaf blades bounce back.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season, specifically when warm season grasses begin to turn green in spring, after determining the appropriate fertilizer type based on your grass type and conducting a pH soil test, and apply the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern while ensuring the lawn is not over-fertilized by checking if the leaf blades bounce back.", "time_sec": 6.004, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 66897, 1318, 2033, 1513, 1278, 10343, 1307, 1278, 13999, 5526, 1044, 13703, 2200, 15701, 5526, 128633,