{"id": "295", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "pred": "Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season, specifically when warm season grasses begin to turn green in spring, after determining the appropriate fertilizer type based on your grass type and conducting a pH soil test, and apply the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern while ensuring the lawn is not over-fertilized by checking if the leaf blades bounce back.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season, specifically when warm season grasses begin to turn green in spring, after determining the appropriate fertilizer type based on your grass type and conducting a pH soil test, and apply the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern while ensuring the lawn is not over-fertilized by checking if the leaf blades bounce back.", "time_sec": 6.047, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 66897, 1318, 2033, 1513, 1278, 10343, 1307, 1278, 13999, 5526, 1044, 13703, 2200, 15701, 5526, 128633, 6396, 1317, 3884, 11223, 1294, 14039, 1044, 2453, 19659, 1278, 10304, 98168, 2658, 4057, 1408, 2143, 23170, 2658, 1321, 38155, 1261, 1274, 1072, 14784, 