{"id": "297", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's gravitational potential energy due to its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy stored in objects due to their deformation. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane's kinetic energy in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, a baseball's kinetic energy due to its fast velocity despite its small mass, and the kinetic energy possessed by objects in motion such as cars, balls, rivers, athletes, amusement park rides, and satellites in orbit.", "pred": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight and a baseball thrown by a pitcher. Examples of potential energy include a car at a certain height (gravitational potential energy) and a satellite in orbit (gravitational potential energy).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight and a baseball thrown by a pitcher. Examples of potential energy include a car at a certain height (gravitational potential energy) and a satellite in orbit (gravitational potential energy).", "time_sec": 4.477, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 28259, 1307, 42683, 6091, 4626, 1420, 94625, 1294, 18034, 1321, 1261, 35167, 29619, 1536, 1261, 68206, 1046, 28259, 1307, 5289, 6091, 4626, 1261, 2382, 1513, 1261, 5029, 5806, 1319, 1103, 6051, 1276, 2535, 5289, 6091, 1041, 1321, 1261, 30042, 1294, 30807, 1319, 1103, 6051, 1276, 2535, 5289, 6091, 1577, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1356, -0.0137, -0.1305, -0.0035, -0.6147, -0.0003, -0.0469, -0.0157, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.826, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0009, -