{"id": "300", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate water. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure that hot water is always available. Demand systems for these pumps can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate water. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure that hot water is always available. Demand systems for these pumps can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "time_sec": 6.479, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1349, 8480, 4180, 27664, 18064, 1710, 1402, 2434, 1317, 3180, 1278, 8480, 4180, 69033, 4087, 8439, 4180, 1046, 2409, 18064, 33716, 12921, 4180, 1294, 1278, 56593, 2595, 1317, 1278, 4180, 69033, 2645, 1261, 1850, 3110, 1044, 11851, 1261, 14118, 9165, 1307, 4180, 2645, 1278, 4180, 69033, 1317, 5