{"id": "301", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how you can make a hot water heater circulate:\n\n1. Install a recirculating pump: As described in passage 3, a recirculating pump can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\n2. Use a demand-based system: According to passage 3, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor. This means that the pump will only run when there is a demand for hot water, rather than constantly running.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to make a hot water heater circulate, but rather describe the concept of circulation and the different types of systems used to achieve it.", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate water. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure that hot water is always available. Demand systems for these pumps can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate water. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure that hot water is always available. Demand systems for these pumps can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "time_sec": 6.561, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "al