{"id": "303", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate water. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure that hot water is always available. Demand systems for these pumps can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A hot water circulation pump can be used to make the hot water heater circulate water. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater to keep it hot and ensure that hot water is always available. Demand systems for these pumps can be controlled by a button, a timer, or a motion sensor.", "time_sec": 6.578, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1349, 8480, 4180, 27664, 18064, 1710, 1402, 2434, 1317, 3180, 1278, 8480, 4180, 69033, 4087, 8439, 4180, 1046, 2409, 18064, 33716, 12921, 4180, 1294, 1278, 56593, 2595, 1317, 1278, 4180, 