{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "Watermelons explode due to the buildup of pressure from gas produced by rotting inside the watermelon, which increases until the skin can no longer hold the gas, causing it to burst.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Watermelons explode due to the buildup of pressure from gas produced by rotting inside the watermelon, which increases until the skin can no longer hold the gas, causing it to burst.", "time_sec": 3.927, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 31988, 1920, 1299, 2232, 54100, 3964, 1317, 1278, 2513, 1318, 61844, 1307, 6909, 1562, 7066, 8077, 1536, 119013, 1302, 6625, 1278, 104924, 129568, 1044, 1799, 11462, 4570, 1278, 9877, 1710, 1836, 7934, 5864, 1278, 7066, 1044, 16312, 1494, 1317, 30621, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1715, -0.0072, -0.1774, -0.0, -0.0023, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.3308, -0.0, -0.0889, -0.4355, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.7122, -0.0709, -0.0511, -0.4247, -0.0358, -0.4622, -0.0, -0.0784, -0.024, -0.3787, -0.0, -0.2887, -0.0732, -0.7523, -0.0164, -0.0001, -0.3949, -0.031, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2072, -0.5069, -0.0371, -0.2266, -0.0658, -0.1299, -0.0, -0.0145, -0.0569, -0.4737], "cumulative_logprob": -6.7299, "norm_logp": -0.1496, "input_len