{"id": "318", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "pred": "You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the Apple App Store), by checking your email for a confirmation from your tax software, or by logging into your tax software account to view the return status.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can check if your taxes were filed by using the IRS2Go mobile application (available for Apple users via the Apple App Store), by checking your email for a confirmation from your tax software, or by logging into your tax software account to view the return status.", "time_sec": 4.777, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3213, 1710, 4206, 1693, 2143, 33257, 1722, 28645, 1536, 2505, 1278, 102753, 1050, 13937, 11396, 5510, 1319, 26731, 1394, 21010, 8616, 