{"id": "335", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes for ticks, as these are favorite hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Wearing gloves is recommended if using fingers to remove the tick.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes for ticks, as these are favorite hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and pull gently and steadily to avoid leaving the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Wearing gloves is recommended if using fingers to remove the tick.", "time_sec": 6.799, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 2012, 15515, 1307, 76849, 1562, 25007, 1044, 4206, 6625, 1321, 7435, 1278, 32961, 1321, 3879, 1278, 5731, 1394, 76849, 1044, 1435, 2576, 1584, 23750