{"id": "351", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "pred": "Company goodwill is the advantage of a business's reputation and its connection with customers, which includes the value of customer attraction to the business's name and reputation. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or products, leading to customer trust, repeat business, and positive word-of-mouth, which in turn creates a business asset known as goodwill.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Company goodwill is the advantage of a business's reputation and its connection with customers, which includes the value of customer attraction to the business's name and reputation. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or products, leading to customer trust, repeat business, and positive word-of-mouth, which in turn creates a business asset known as goodwill.", "time_sec": 7.595, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 10889, 3683, 27142, 1395, 1278, 12772, 1307, 1261, 6170, 1681, 30200, 1321, 2246, 7936, 1454, 17365, 1044, 1799, 6987, 1278, 2632, 1307, 14146, 41570, 1317, 1278, 6170, 1681, 2564, 1321, 30200, 1046, 2157, 1395, 4023, 3147, 1494, 11462, 1278, 14146, 4469, 1044, 77311, 3992, 17412, 1044, 127809, 41914, 1044, 1321, 127809, 7147, 69519, 1046, 13649, 27142, 1395, 6254, 2200, 1261, 6170, 8222, 3683, 4810, 1505, 8066, 1044, 8924, 1317, 14146, 12319, 1044, 21788, 6170, 1044, 1321, 6818, 3541, 13144, 3049, 4519, 1044, 1799, 1294, 3884, 21622, 1261, 6170, 24596, 4629, 1435, 3683, 27142, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.285, -0.0493, -0.2148, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.2676, -0.042, -0.8733, -0.4223, -0.0995, -0.0028, -0.0774, -0.0001, -0.0181, -0.9637, -0.1279, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0065, -0.9562, -1.2936, -0.2467, -0.9884, -0.0145, -0.1462, -0.0519, -1.1806, -0.0286, -0.6625, -0.3657, -0.0048, -0.0007, -0.0288, -0.4606, -0.1174, -0.0085, -0.0049, -0.0988, -0.0271, -0.0907, -0.2724, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0448, -0.0299, -0.0117, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0247, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0038, -0.0077, -0.0032, -0.0, -0.0913, -0.8296, -0.0008, -0.4901, -0.2586, -0.006, -0.091, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.0026, -0.0088, -0.0001, -0.0224, -0.0013, -0.0007, -0.0422, -0.0259, -0.0, -0.0673, -0.0004, -0.166, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0352, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4005, -0.0338, -0.1986, -0.0001, -0.437, -0.005, -0.5185, -0.0, -0.6691, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0003, -0.045, -0.215], "cumulative_logprob": -15.2992, "norm_logp": -0.1561, "input_len": 367, "output_tokens": 98, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.33, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "353", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, goodwill can be understood as a business asset that comes from a positive reputation and good connections with customers. It can be increased through providing good service or products, resulting in loyal and repeat customers who also spread positive reviews about the business. This goodwill attracts new customers, investors, and future buyers, making it an important factor in business success.", "pred": "Company goodwill is the advantage of a business's reputation and its connection with customers, which includes the value of customer attraction to the business's name and reputation. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or products, leading to customer trust, repeat business, and positive word-of-mouth, which in turn creates a business asset known as goodwill.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Company goodwill is the advantage of a business's reputation and its connection with customers, which includes the value of customer attraction to the business's name and reputation. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or products, leading to customer trust, repeat business, and positive word-of-mouth, which in turn creates a business asset known as goodwill.", "time_sec": 7.585, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 10889, 3683, 27142, 1395, 1278, 12772, 1307, 1261, 6170, 1681, 3020