{"id": "354", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "pred": "Company goodwill is the advantage of a business's reputation and its connection with customers, which includes the value of customer attraction to the business's name and reputation. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or products, leading to customer trust, repeat business, and positive word-of-mouth, which in turn creates a business asset known as goodwill.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Company goodwill is the advantage of a business's reputation and its connection with customers, which includes the value of customer attraction to the business's name and reputation. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or products, leading to customer trust, repeat business, and positive word-of-mouth, which in turn creates a business asset known as goodwill.", "time_sec": 7.451, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 10889, 3683, 27142, 1395, 1278, 12772, 1307, 1261, 6170, 1681, 30200, 1321, 2246, 7936, 1454, 17365, 1044, 1799, 6987, 1278, 2632, 1307, 14146, 41570, 1317, 1278, 6170, 1681, 2564, 1321, 30200, 1046, 2157, 1395, 4023, 3147, 1494, 11462, 1278, 14146, 4469, 1044, 77311, 3992, 17412, 1044, 127809, 41914, 1044, 1321, 127809, 7147, 69519, 1046, 13649, 27142, 1395, 6254, 2200, 1261, 6170, 8222, 3683, 4810, 1505, 8066, 1044, 8924, 1317, 14146, 12319, 1044, 21788, 6170, 1044, 1321, 6818, 3541, 13144, 3049, 4519, 1044, 1799, 1294, 3884, 21622, 1261, 6170, 24596, 4629, 1435, 3683, 27142, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.285, -0.0493, -0.2148, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.2676, -0.042, -0.8733, -0.4223, -0.0995, -0.0028, -0.0774, -0.0001, -0.0181, -0.9637, -0.1279, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0065, -0.9562, -1.2936, -0.2467, -0.9884, -0.0145, -0.1462, -0.0519, -1.1806, -0.0286, -0.6625, -0.3657, -0.0048, -0.0007, -0.0288, -0.4606, -0.1174, -0.0085, -0.0049, -0.0988, -0.0271, -0.0907, -0.2724, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0448, -0.0299, -0.0117, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0247, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0038, -0.0077, -0.0032, -0.0, -0.0913, -0.8296, -0.0008, -0.4901, -0.2586, -0.006, -0.091, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.0026, -0.0088, -0.0001, -0.0224, -0.0013, -0.0007, -0.0422, -0.0259, -0.0, -0.0673, -0.0004, -0.166, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0352, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4005, -0.0338, -0.1986, -0.0001, -0.437, -0.005, -0.5185, -0.0, -0.6691, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0003, -0.045, -0.215], "cumulative_logprob": -15.2992, "norm_logp": -0.1561, "input_len": 367, "output_tokens": 98, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.74, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "G