{"id": "367", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a rock is defined as the hard material of the earth's crust that is normally exposed on the surface or underlying the soil. On the other hand, a stone is described as a smaller piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The passages also mention that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, while rocks cannot. Therefore, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size, with rocks being larger and stones being smaller and easier to handle.", "pred": "A rock is a large piece of stone that is difficult to carry in the hand, while a stone is a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones are made from rocks. Stones can be easily pelted, but one cannot do so with rocks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A rock is a large piece of stone that is difficult to carry in the hand, while a stone is a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones are made from rocks. Stones can be easily pelted, but one cannot do so with rocks.", "time_sec": 5.673, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1349, 9091, 1395, 1261, 4329, 13079, 1307, 15551, 1455, 1395, 6593, 1317, 10739, 1294, 1278, 2786, 1044, 3016, 1261, 15551, 1395, 1261, 3709, 13079, 1505, 2135, 1098, 2268, 1455, 1710, 1402, 9523, 1294, 1278, 2786, 1046, 101518, 1584, 3214, 1307, 10752, 39696, 1044, 1321, 39696, 1584, 3214, 1562, 34176, 1046, 71696, 1710, 1402, 10421, 1274, 3656, 1286, 1044, 1809, 1925, 6560, 1653, 1878, 1454, 