{"id": "368", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size. Rocks are typically larger and more massive than stones, which are smaller and more fragmented.\n\nPassage 1 states that rocks are often used to refer to something solid, large, and grounded, such as a mountain or palisade, while stones are often used to refer to small pieces of rock or pebbles. Passage 2 defines rocks as the hard material of the earth's crust that is exposed on the surface of the earth or underlying the soil, while stones are smaller fragments of rock that can be carried in the hand.\n\nPassage 3 further clarifies the distinction by stating that rocks are made up of smaller stones, while stones are made from rocks. Additionally, rocks are described as being difficult to carry in the hand, while stones are small enough to be carried easily.\n\nIn summary, while both rocks and stones are made of the same material, they differ in size and usage. Rocks are generally larger and more massive, while stones are smaller and more fragmented.", "pred": "A rock is a large piece of stone that is difficult to carry in the hand, while a stone is a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones are made from rocks. Stones can be easily pelted, but one cannot do so with rocks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: A rock is a large piece of stone that is difficult to carry in the hand, while a stone is a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Rocks are made of smaller stones, and stones are made from rocks. Stones can be easily pelted, but one cannot do so with rocks.", "time_sec": 5.763, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": 