{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps based on the passages:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps based on the passages:  \n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of row and column headings to select all cells in the worksheet (passage 3, step 1).  \n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group, then click on the Sort option (passage 3, step 2).  \n3. In the Sort window, select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., the Product column in column B) from the \"Sort By\" drop-down menu (passage 2, \"select the data that you wish to sort by\" and passage 3, step 3).  \n4. Choose \"A to Z\" (alphabetical order) as the sort order and click OK (passage 2, \"select Custom Sort from the popup menu\" and \"sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z)\").  \n\nThis process sorts the data alphabetically based on the selected column, as demonstrated in the example where the Product column (column B) is sorted A to Z.", "time_sec": 18.133, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids