{"id": "382", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps based on the passages:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps based on the passages:  \n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of row and column headings to select all cells in the worksheet (passage 3, step 1).  \n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group, then click on the Sort option (passage 3, step 2).  \n3. In the Sort window, select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., the Product column in column B) from the \"Sort By\" drop-down menu (passage 2, \"select the data that you wish to sort by\" and passage 3, step 3).  \n4. Choose \"A to Z\" (alphabetical order) as the sort order and click OK (passage 2, \"select Custom Sort from the popup menu\" and \"sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z)\").  \n\nThis process sorts the data alphabetically based on the selected column, as demonstrated in the example where the Product column (column B) is sorted A to Z.", "time_sec": 18.199, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 55428, 1420, 35367, 15241, 46198, 2981, 1044, 1636, 1710, 2685, 2576, 9578, 4057, 1408, 1278, 42679, 1058, 1256, 1010, 1049, 1046, 30476, 1408, 1278, 20088, 3797, 8305, 1513, 127