{"id": "387", "question": "what is the normal b natriuretic peptide", "gt": "The normal B-type Natriuretic Peptide (BNP) refers to a low amount of the BNP hormone found in the blood, produced by the heart as a measure of how well it is working. The exact normal values are not stated but are suggested to be a guide and can vary based on factors like age and gender, with values tending to increase with age and being higher in women. High levels of BNP are indicative of heart failure, with higher levels at diagnosis suggesting a more severe condition. Conversely, low levels tend to exclude heart failure.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.627, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 71297, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.3447, -0.002, -0.7933, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0046], "cumulative_logprob": -1.1453, "norm_logp": -0.0954, "input_len": 517, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.08, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
