{"id": "434", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean tarnished jewelry at home\":\n\nTo clean tarnished jewelry at home, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth in the solution. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse it in cool water and buff it with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water and apply it with a soft, lint-free cloth. You can also use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl and submerging the jewelry in it. Let it sit for a while, then remove and rinse it with cool water. Be sure to use a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, for items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water, dip a soft cloth in the solution, rub the jewelry, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, create a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water, wet the silver, and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. Alternatively, pour two cups of hot water into a bowl, add enough salt to cover the jewelry, and submerge the jewelry in the solution; this gentle method removes tarnish without abrading the silver, but ensure gemstones are not affected by saltwater.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, for items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water, dip a soft cloth in the solution, rub the jewelry, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, create a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water, wet the silver, and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. Alternatively, 