{"id": "436", "question": "how to find someone in france", "gt": "To find someone in France, you can use the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person in the \"Nom\" field and optionally enter their first name in the \"Prenom\" field. If you know the address, you can enter it in the \"Ou\" section. Leave it blank if you don't know the address. Click on \"Trouver\" to search for the name. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number of the matching listings.", "pred": "To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (Pages Jaunes) by visiting www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the \"Nom\" field and their first name in the \"Prenom\" field. If you know their address, input it in the \"Ou\" section; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. For searching in Paris and its suburbs, use \"IDF\" (Ile de France) in the \"Dept\" or region field instead of \"Paris.\" Additionally, you can send an email or letter to the town hall in the city where the person was born, especially if you have lost contact for over ten or twenty years. Including the person's middle name can also make the search easier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (Pages Jaunes) by visiting www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the \"Nom\" field and their first name in the \"Prenom\" field. If you know their address, input it in the \"Ou\" section; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. For searching in Paris and its suburbs, use \"IDF\" (Ile de France) in the \"Dept\" or region field instead of \"Paris.\" Additionally, you can send an email or letter to the town hall in the city where the person was born, especially if you have lost contact for over ten or twenty years. Including the person's m