{"id": "440", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help in the regeneration of the forest. Fires consume dead and decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Jack pines rely on fire to spread their seeds. They produce seratonous (resin-filled) cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to open and the seeds to fall or blow out. Furthermore, fires can disrupt the growth of other trees like spruce, providing an advantage to the more fire-tolerant jack pines and allowing them to proliferate.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pines in the Canadian boreal forest, where they are a key pioneer species that relies on fire for seed dispersal and regeneration.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pines in the Canadian boreal forest, where they are a key pioneer species that relies on fire for seed dispersal and regeneration.", "time_sec": 6.918, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 25119, 47554, 1584, 27881, 1317, 1383, 112996, 2479, 59131, 1274, 2783, 3147, 2127, 34828, 1278, 24001, 1294, 1278, 1383, 112996, 1039, 2169, 22755, 1718, 1319, 1770, 1259, 77187, 1041, 112901, 1044, 16312, 2424, 1317, 2915, 3432, 1321, 8021, 2034, 30692, 1044, 1799, 2430, 6962, 1505, 27137, 1848, 1317, 14975, 1875, 6762, 1059, 1593, 1395, 13703, 10656, 1394, 59131, 1274, 2783, 1294, 1278, 17267, 35080, 1279, 17144, 1044, 2478, 2127, 1584, 1261, 3844, 82204, 6584, 1455, 48527, 1408, 7482, 1394, 15173, 90589, 1321, 44360, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.6871, -0.0202, -0.2159, -0.0001, -0.2139, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0046, -0.0009, -0.0006, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0058, -0.2462, -0.3526, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0132, -0.0019, -0.6234, -0.6139, -0.0205, -0.7233, -0.0208, -0.0002, -0.3347, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.086, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0021, -0.0029, -0.2331, -0.0, -0.0375, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0125, -0.1203, -0.0008, -0.2511, -0.0051, -0.5226, -0.315, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0026, -0.1218, -0.2985, -0.0127, -0.0, -0.9754, -0.528, -0.7348, -1.1457, -0.47, -0.1718, -0.3923, -0.5898, -0.0, -0.1612, -0.0035, -0.0449, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4619, -0.0147, -0.2134, -0.0979, -0.9309, -0.0374, -0.0805, -0.0, -0.5503, -0.4827, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0023, -0.012, -0.0407, -0.3486, -0.0075, -0.159, -0.0023], "cumulative_logprob": -14.7882, "norm_logp": -0.168, "input_len": 408, "output_tokens": 88, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.85, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "443", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\n\n1. Fire helps to clear the way for new growth by consuming dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, creating a clean slate for seed germination and seedling establishment (Passage 2).\n2. Jack pine seeds are adapted to fire, as they are stored in serotinous cones that only open after a fire has melted the resin holding them closed. This allows the seeds to disperse and establish new populations (Passage 2).\n3. Fire can create a favorable environment for jack pine and aspen regrowth by reducing competition from other tree species, such as spruce, which have better access to sunlight while shading the other trees (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, forest fires can benefit jack pines by providing a means of seed dispersal and creating conditions that promote their growth and regeneration.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pines in the Canadian boreal forest, where they are a key pioneer species that relies on fire for seed dispersal and regeneration.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they melt the resin in the conifers' seratonous (resin-filled) cones, causing them to pop open and release their seeds, which then fall or blow out to enable new growth; this is specifically noted for jack pines in the Canadian boreal forest, where they are a key pioneer species that relies on fire for seed dispersal and regeneration.", "time_sec": 6.877, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transfo