{"id": "467", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "gt": "Hiking as a hobby has numerous benefits for both the body and the mind. It is an inexpensive and accessible activity that can be enjoyed by individuals of all fitness levels. Hiking allows people to explore and discover beautiful natural areas, promoting a deeper connection with the environment. It also has positive effects on mental health, reducing stress and anxiety. Additionally, hiking is a cardiovascular activity that can improve overall fitness and reduce the risk of heart disease. Exposure to sunshine during hiking can also increase vitamin D levels in the body. Overall, hiking offers a wide range of benefits for individuals seeking physical and mental well-being.", "pred": "Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, is inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels, promotes mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels via sun exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and improving fitness, and combats stress and anxiety by connecting individuals with nature, as noted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Outdoor hiking offers numerous benefits for both body and mind, is inexpensive and accessible to all fitness levels, promotes mental health through varied exercise compared to gym activities, increases vitamin D levels via sun exposure, supports cardiovascular health by reducing heart disease risk and improving fitness, and combats stress and anxiety by connecting individuals with nature, as noted by Gregory A. Miller of the American Hiking Society.", "time_sec": 6.365, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "a