{"id": "471", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and deodorized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and deodorized.", "time_sec": 6.391, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17460, 2611, 94317, 10673, 1395, 3214, 1562, 27998, 94317, 20370, 1321, 1934, 1261, 2738, 26548, 2862, 1307, 1032, 1052, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1044, 6187, 1494, 13684, 1394, 2738, 70752, 37173, 1044, 3016, 1457, 3166, 2611, 94317, 10673, 1395, 3214, 1562, 14420, 94317, 36107, 1044, 1934, 1261, 4953, 26548, 2862, 1307, 1032, 1051, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1044, 1321, 77311, 1261, 23852, 94317, 52288, 1321, 88769, 3964, 1317, 3144, 1457, 99967, 1321, 131