{"id": "473", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and deodorized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and deodorized.", "time_sec": 6.332, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17460, 2611, 94317, 10673, 1395, 3214, 1562, 27998, 94317, 20370, 1321, 1934, 1261, 2738, 26548, 2862, 1307, 1032, 1052, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1044, 6187, 1494, 13684, 1394, 2738, 70752, 37173, 1044, 3016, 1457, 3166, 2611, 94317, 10673, 1