{"id": "474", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and deodorized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F, and retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma due to being unprocessed and deodorized.", "time_sec": 6.296, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 17460, 2611, 94317, 10673, 1395, 3214, 1562, 27998, 94317, 20370, 1321, 1934, 1261,