{"id": "478", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Passage 3 provides information on how to change your address with the U.S. Postal Service. You can visit their website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit a form at a U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely with the Postal Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, and it uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely with the Postal Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, and it uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.", "time_sec": 12.735, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 