{"id": "479", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "To change your US postal address, you can visit the official website of the U.S. Postal Service, fill out an online form, or contact their call center. The process is fast and versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS. It's important to note that you can also use this feature to have your business mail forwarded to a new address due to a permanent move or temporary relocation. The process involves submitting either an online form or filling out and submitting a physical form at any U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely with the Postal Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, and it uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Change your U.S. postal service address quickly and securely with the Postal Change of Address service, which can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS, and it uses the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can change your address by visiting https://moversguide.usps.com/ (with a $1 identity validation charge), calling the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or filling out and submitting PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any 