{"id": "492", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, there are several ways to track who likes your tweets:\n\n1. Favotter.net and Favstar.fm - These websites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets and which tweets have been favorited by multiple users. (Passage 1)\n2. Using a web-based website - There are websites that allow you to check Twitter users who favorite tweets. (Passage 2)\n3. On Twitter - You can set up your account settings to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is: You can use Favotter.net, Favstar.fm, or a web-based website to track who likes your tweets, or you can set up your Twitter account settings to receive email notifications.", "pred": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which track favorited tweets and show you who has favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you.", "time_sec": 3.969, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3213, 1710, 5584, 2274, 26648, 2143, 69417, 1536, 2505, 39307, 2479, 89437, 1360, 1397, 9592, 1321, 89437, 19241, 3175, 1109, 1044, 1799, 6933, 8209, 2770, 88357, 1321, 2629, 1636, 2274, 1934, 8209, 2770, 2143, 88357, 1505, 1278, 2879, 88357, 1435, 1636, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0666, -0.0032, -0.0914, -0.0001, -0.1517, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.1281, -0.0007, -0.0008, -0.0619, -0.6289, -