{"id": "497", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that salary exchange is a way for employees to give up part of their salary in exchange for a pension contribution made by their employer. The salary that is waived is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution, minus any additional contributions. The employer then pays the corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to potentially save money through reduced national insurance contributions.", "pred": "Salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money, as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary, and employees receive pension contributions without directly paying for them from their salary. For example, in the context of the University Scheme for Superannuation (USS), the regular contribution is 7.5% of pay, and for the University Scheme for Pension and Retirement Benefits (USPAS), it is 9%. The salary waived by the employee is equal to the value of their regular pension contribution, excluding additional contributions (AVCs), and the employer matches this amount by paying it into the relevant pension scheme.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money, as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary, and employees receive pension contributions without directly paying for them from their salary. For example, in the context of the University Scheme for Superannuation (USS), the regular contribution is 7.5% of pay, and for the University Scheme for Pension and Retirement Benefits (USPAS), it is 9%. The salary waived by the employee is equal to the value of their regular pension contribution, excluding additional contributions (AVCs), and the employer matches this amount by paying it into the relevant pension scheme.", "time_sec": 12.451, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 6424, 1760, 13591, 48863, 24042, 24441, 1420, 22054, 99430, 1317, 5628, 2015, 1805, 1307, 2034, 40826, 1505, 29255, 1294, 13591, 1394, 1261, 48863, 20341, 3214, 1536, 2034, 45195, 1046, 2409, 21200, 9985, 2960, 53032, 1321, 17942, 1317, 8704, 8551, 1044, 1435, 53032, 6012, 4953, 5805, 52735, 4988, 82671, 1319, 1078, 6048, 1115, 1041, 3964, 1317, 1278, 7896, 40826, 1044, 1321, 17942, 10477, 48863, 24042, 3816, 7655, 33235, 1394, 2424, 1562, 2034, 40826, 1046, 2898, 3336, 1044, 1294, 1278, 5315, 1307, 1278, 5189, 65953, 1394, 9153, 1980, 65656, 1319, 125878, 1574, 1278, 8385, 18945, 1395, 1032, 1055, 1046, 1053, 1037, 1307, 6012, 1044, 1321, 1394, 1278, 5189, 65953, 1394, 1390, 4574, 1321, 16286, 21385, 109368, 1319, 5507, 1080, 6003, 1574, 1494, 1395, 1032, 1057, 14082, 1531, 40826, 8411, 3474, 1536, 1278, 22054, 1395, 9196, 1317, 1278, 2632, 1307, 2034, 8385, 48863, 18945, 1044, 55063, 7481, 24042, 1319, 1065, 20500, 1115, 1574, 1321, 1278, 45195, 14175, 1593, 5647, 1536, 33235, 1494, 2203, 1278, 11157, 48863, 17676, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0679, -0.0231, -0.0616, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4198, -0.0002, -0.3178, -0.0106, -0.0038, -0.2126, -0.0, -0.0087, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0636, -0.0, -0.0266, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.164, -0.0005, -0.0078, -0.0082, -0.0, -0.0789, 0.0, -0