{"id": "501", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin are primarily genetic/hereditary factors and hormonal shifts in the body. Diet and poor hygiene/topical applications have a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin. Combination skin, which is a mix of oily and dry/normal areas, can also contribute to oily skin in certain areas such as the T-zone.", "pred": "Factors that cause oily skin include genetics (heredity), hormonal shifts in the body, and potentially diet (though diet is described as having a limited effect and not causing oily skin directly). The passages state that oily skin is hereditary (\"if your mom or dad has oily skin, chances are you will, too\"), can be influenced by hormonal shifts (\"if your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genes and more to do with hormonal shifts\"), and that diet \"can aggravate acne, but it doesn't cause oily skin\" and \"has a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Factors that cause oily skin include genetics (heredity), hormonal shifts in the body, and potentially diet (though diet is described as having a limited effect and not causing oily skin directly). The passages state that oily skin is hereditary (\"if your mom or dad has oily skin, chances are you will, too\"), can be influenced by hormonal shifts (\"if your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genes and more to do with hormonal shifts\"), and that diet \"can aggravate acne, but it doesn't cause oily skin\" and \"has a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin.\"", "time_sec": 10.244, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010,