{"id": "507", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "pred": "The tropical rainforest floor features herbs and mushrooms that grow there, along with vines and ferns that help connect the various layers of the biome. Bananas also grow on vines in this biome. Due to the heat and moisture, plants and animals that die in this location rot quickly, and their decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The tropical rainforest floor features herbs and mushrooms that grow there, along with vines and ferns that help connect the various layers of the biome. Bananas also grow on vines in this biome. Due to the heat and moisture, plants and animals that die in this location rot quickly, and their decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "time_sec": 6.12, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 24170, 17378, 106761, 11237, 6971, 81991, 1321, 125404, 1455, 4492, 2156, 1044, 4837