{"id": "508", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "pred": "Sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion, while Porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a larger portion of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-Bone steaks. The Porterhouse is a larger version of the T-Bone steak, as it is carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion, while Porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a larger portion of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-Bone steaks. The Porterhouse is a larger version of the T-Bone steak, as it is carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin.", "time_sec": 6.883, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 13704, 1906, 1259, 3995, 1489, 1395, 6945, 1562, 1278, 2595, 1307, 1278, 11386, 1044, 13703, 1278, 18268, 2595, 7575, 1044, 3016, 49094, 15454, 3995, 1489, 1395, 6945, 1562, 4514, 2595, 1408, 1278, 18942, 1906, 1259, 1321, 8688, 1261, 9039, 7575, 1307, 1278, 44441, 1906, 1259, 1505, 2339, 2186, 5496, 1317, 1353, 5630, 1774, 3