{"id": "521", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA raffle is a game of chance where participants buy tickets with a unique number, and a prize is awarded to the holder of the winning ticket drawn at random. In a reverse raffle, the process is similar, but the tickets are numbered from 1 to approximately 55, and tables consist of 20 individuals, constituting one complete ticket at $1000, with two $500 prizes available. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, with 50% going to the winner of the random draw and the remaining 50% going to a charitable cause.\n\nTherefore, raffles typically involve buying tickets with unique numbers, and a random draw determines the winner, with a percentage of the proceeds often going to a charitable cause.", "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets, where each ticket has a number (e.g., 1 to 55 in a reverse raffle), and a portion of the ticket sales (gross proceeds) is allocated to prizes. In a reverse raffle, a table of 20 individuals (one complete ticket at $1000) participates in drawings for $500 prizes (early bird and first ticket pulled). In a 50-50 draw, 50% of ticket sales go to the winner of a random draw, and the remaining 50% is set aside for charity. Tickets may include additional benefits like drinks and dinner, and separate cash tip board raffles offer chances to win $10,000.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Raffles work by selling tickets, where each ticket has a number (e.g., 1 to 55 in a reverse raffle), and a portion of the ticket sales (gross proceeds) is allocated to prizes. In a reverse raffle, a table of 20 individuals (one complete ticket at $1000) participates in drawings for $500 prizes (early bird and first ticket pulled). In a 50-50 draw, 50% of ticket sales go to the winner of a random draw, and the remaining 50% is set aside for charity. Tickets may include additional benefits like drinks and dinner, and separate cash tip board raffles offer chances to win $10,000.", "time_sec": 11.839, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 70588, 2013, 2196, 1536, 28342, 44620, 1044, 2478, 2744, 30191, 1934, 1261, 2782, 1319, 1101, 3596, 3109, 1032, 1049, 1317, 1032, 1053, 1053, 1294, 1261, 16448, 50665, 1282, 1574, 1321, 1261, 7575, 1307, 1278, 30191, 15638, 1319, 1103, 3275, 44015, 1041, 1395, 32873, 1317, 99941, 1046, 1656, 1261, 16448, 50665, 1282, 1044, 1261, 4234, 1307, 1032, 1050, 1048, 8833, 1319, 1774, 7662, 30191, 1513, 1659, 1049, 1048, 1048, 1048, 1041, 105029, 1294, 33549, 1394, 1659, 1053, 1048, 1048, 99941, 1319, 90132, 16409, 1321, 2158, 30191, 13538, 1577, 1656, 1261, 1032, 1053, 1048, 1045, 1053, 1048, 7277, 1044, 1032, 1053, 1048, 1037, 1307, 30191, 15638, 1974, 1317, 1278, 24340, 1307, 1261, 6974, 7277, 1044, 1321, 1278, 11829, 1032, 1053, 1048, 1037, 1395, 2016, 27230, 1394, 48205, 1046, 1353, 23149, 2188, 4626, 7481, 15021, 2479, 47394, 1321, 24837, 1044, 1321, 9960, 22506, 11210, 9710, 50665, 2013, 6266, 34944, 1317, 6419, 1659, 1049, 1048, 1044, 1048, 1048, 1048, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.189, -0.0059, -0.3627, -0.0096, -0.1351, -0.018, -0.3262, -0.623, -0.7451, -1.0453, -0.2602, -0.0168, -0.0224, -0.0357, -0.7392, -1.1898, -0.2736, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.5603, -0.0006, -0.0123, -0.0962, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.9349, -0.1693, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0, -1.2005, -0.0877, -0.5503, -0.8401, -0.0752, -0.0361, -0.1459, -0.0261, -0.4185, -0.6327, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.1114, -0.4047, -0.2705, -0.3627, -0.1915, -0.5383, -0.0135, -0.2133, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0093, -0.5768, -0.0991, -0.0131, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2065, -0.9362, -1.179, -0.5913, -0.0002, -0.34