{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "To create employee schedules, first make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper for this purpose. Print out copies for employees or send schedules via email, and keep a master schedule for making changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create schedules for multiple employees, allowing for easy template reuse as the business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To create employee schedules, first make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper for this purpose. Print out copies for employees or send schedules via email, and keep a master schedule for making changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create schedules for multiple employees, allowing for easy template reuse as the business grows.", "time_sec": 7.739, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [10