{"id": "610", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "pred": "To create employee schedules, first make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper for this purpose. Print out copies for employees or send schedules via email, and keep a master schedule for making changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create schedules for multiple employees, allowing for easy template reuse as the business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To create employee schedules, first make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper for this purpose. Print out copies for employees or send schedules via email, and keep a master schedule for making changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create schedules for multiple employees, allowing for easy template reuse as the business grows.", "time_sec": 7.87, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "au