{"id": "611", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to create an employee schedule:\n\n1. Talk to a lawyer about work laws: It is important to understand the legal requirements for creating an employee schedule, including paying overtime for hours worked beyond 40 per week. Additionally, there may be other laws to consider, such as restrictions for employees under the age of 18.\n2. Use scheduling software or a simple word processing program: You can create an employee schedule using scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or even a sheet of paper. Make a list of all employees and their duties, and create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\n3. Print or send schedules to employees: Once you have created the schedule, print out copies for each employee or send them to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule for making any changes. If you are using a digital tool, you can easily edit and share the schedule with employees.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to create an employee schedule, such as setting up the schedule format, determining pay rates, or communicating the schedule to employees.", "pred": "To create employee schedules, first make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper for this purpose. Print out copies for employees or send schedules via email, and keep a master schedule for making changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create schedules for multiple employees, allowing for easy template reuse as the business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To create employee schedules, first make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Then, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper for this purpose. Print out copies for employees or send schedules via email, and keep a master schedule for making changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create schedules for multiple employees, allowing for easy template reuse as the business grows.", "time_sec": 7.734, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 4305, 22054, 71871, 1044, 2158, 3180, 1261, 2951, 1307, 1747, 17942, 1321, 1278, 31879, 2127, 1710, 3142, 1046, 6830, 1044, 3180, 1261, 14837, 1307, 1278, 2196, 5072, 1321, 1278, 7700, 1394, 2744, 3950, 1046, 3213, 1710, 2210, 52579, 9314, 1044, 1261, 3541, 8673, 3467, 1044, 1505, 1261, 15241, 1307, 7873, 1394, 1593, 10485, 1046, 24983, 1848, 22720, 1394, 17942, 1505, 8160, 71871, 5059, 8686, 1044, 1321, 5807, 1261, 12743, 21027, 1394, 6187, 5266, 1046, 14560, 35367, 1710, 1402, 2434, 1317, 4305, 71871, 1394, 6245, 17942, 1044, 15249, 1394, 9517, 10968, 58290, 1435, 1278, 6170, 48064, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1385, -0.0299, -0.1543, -0.8783, -0.0209, -0.0, -0.0267, -0.1623, -0.0173, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0065, -0.0001, -0.2289, -0.0, -0.0028, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.6961, -0.0786, -0.0505, -0.2473, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0308, -0.0627, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0256, -0.0027, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0186, -0.0436, -0.0004, -0.0033, -0.0053, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0055, -0.0106, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.2061, -0.0006, -0.496, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2393, -0.0, -0.5249, -0.0304, -1.0713, -0.0198, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0233, -0.0514, -0.264, -0.0008, -0.2457, -0.0021, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.1123, -0.0455, -0.0178, -0.0341, -0.0764, -0.0001, -0.0216, -0.0028, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.2071, -0.0008, 0.0, -0.0, -0