{"id": "632", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "pred": "The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences. \n\n**Similarities**:  \n- Both systems maintain homeostasis by coordinating and regulating cellular, tissue, organ, and systemic activities.  \n- Both utilize chemical messengers (neurotransmitters in the nervous system, hormones in the endocrine system) for signal transmission.  \n- Both are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.  \n\n**Differences**:  \n- **Structure**: The nervous system consists of interconnected neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of discrete, unconnected glands.  \n- **Transmission**: The nervous system uses electrochemical pulses (nerve impulses) for rapid, direct signal transmission. The endocrine system relies on hormones released into the circulatory system, resulting in slower, widespread signal distribution.  \n- **Physical Connectivity**: Nervous system cells are physically interconnected, whereas endocrine organs operate independently without direct physical connections.  \n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 14.673, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 25199, 2663, 1321, 80583, 2663, 9730, 3844, 46699, 1321, 23892, 11074, 7938, 1046, 1032, 1267, 1438, 69656, 2754, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 6467, 7766, 54022, 1536, 110019, 1321, 39361, 16885, 1044, 9392, 1044, 3338, 1044, 1321, 27682, 9216, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 40013, 11883, 8871, 23740, 1319, 1546, 3317, 5207, 3674, 3701, 1294, 1278, 25199, 2663, 1044, 52832, 1294, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1041, 1394, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 1584, 30317, 1536, 8289, 17887, 12630, 1046, 1256, 1267, 1438, 1068, 13831, 3224, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 50947, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 15730, 1307, 78490, 45375, 3459, 1044, 3016, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1395, 16815, 1307, 33123, 1044, 1457, 31390, 65067, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 6881, 5061, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 8942, 60732, 43812, 1319, 2356, 1672, 118855, 1041, 1394, 8744, 1044, 3236, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1531, 80583, 2663, 48527, 1408, 52832, 7358, 2203, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 1044, 9903, 1294, 37625, 1044, 28759, 4987, 7507, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 85418, 26290, 3078, 5450, 87187, 1718, 2663, 3459, 1584, 33599, 78490, 1044, 11275, 80583, 31918, 21590, 22272, 3816, 3236, 8137, 20053, 1046, 1256, 1267, 62386, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.3645, -0.0491, -0.5336, -0.0776, -0.0173, -0.0513, -0.0183, -0.0, -0.4199, -0.287, -0.0006, -0.1907, -0.5121, -0.3378, -0.0001, -0.3712, -1.1712, -0.0022, -0.1857, -0.001, -0.0436, -0.8916, -0.2131, -0.0, -0.5981, -0.001, -0.0046, -0.0255, -0.0937, -0.0003, -0.1585, -0.0032, -0.0, -0.6148, -0.0102, -0.0, -0.0, -0.029, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0963, -0.0001, -0.2458, -0.0032, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.5676, -0.7014, -0.0, -0.0, -0.3282, -0.0106, -0.0005, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0, -0