{"id": "633", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system have both similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n1. Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis and coordinating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers play a crucial role in both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while chemical hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system utilizes interconnected cells to transmit signals, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "pred": "The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences. \n\n**Similarities**:  \n- Both systems maintain homeostasis by coordinating and regulating cellular, tissue, organ, and systemic activities.  \n- Both utilize chemical messengers (neurotransmitters in the nervous system, hormones in the endocrine system) for signal transmission.  \n- Both are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.  \n\n**Differences**:  \n- **Structure**: The nervous system consists of interconnected neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of discrete, unconnected glands.  \n- **Transmission**: The nervous system uses electrochemical pulses (nerve impulses) for rapid, direct signal transmission. The endocrine system relies on hormones released into the circulatory system, resulting in slower, widespread signal distribution.  \n- **Physical Connectivity**: Nervous system cells are physically interconnected, whereas endocrine organs operate independently without direct physical connections.  \n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 14.721, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 25199, 2663, 1321, 80583, 2663, 9730, 3844, 46699, 1321, 23892, 11074, 7938, 1046, 1032, 1267, 1438, 69656, 2754, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 6467, 7766, 54022, 1536, 110019, 1321, 39361, 16885, 1044, 9392, 1044, 3338, 1044, 1321, 27682, 9216, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 40013, 11883, 8871, 23740, 1319, 1546, 3317, 5207, 3674, 3701, 1294, 1278, 25199, 2663, 1044, 52832, 1294, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1041, 1394, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 1584, 30317, 1536, 8289, 17887, 12630, 1046, 1256, 1267, 1438, 1068, 13831, 3224, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 50947, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 15730, 1307, 78490, 45375, 3459, 1044, 3016, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1395, 16815, 1307, 33123, 1044, 1457, 31390, 65067, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 6881, 5061, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 8942, 60732, 43812, 1319, 2356, 1672, 118855, 1041, 1394, 8744, 1044, 3236, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1531, 80583, 2663, 48527, 1408, 52832, 7358, 2203, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 1044, 9903, 1294, 37625, 1044, 28759, 4987, 7507, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 85418, 26290, 3078, 5450, 87187, 1718, 2663, 3459, 1584, 33599, 78490, 1044, 11275, 80583, 31918, 21590, 22272, 3816, 3236, 8137, 20053, 1046, 1256, 1267, 62386, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.3645, -0.0491, -0.5336, -0.0776, -0.0173, -0.0513, -0.0183, -0.0, -0.4199, -0.287, -0.0006, -0.1907