{"id": "634", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the nervous system and endocrine system have some similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n- Both systems are responsible for maintaining homeostasis in the body.\n- Both systems use chemical messengers to coordinate and regulate the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Negative feedback mechanisms are used to regulate both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses while transmission in the endocrine system is done through chemicals called hormones.\n- The nervous system is a continuous network of interconnected cells while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs that are not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "pred": "The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences. \n\n**Similarities**:  \n- Both systems maintain homeostasis by coordinating and regulating cellular, tissue, organ, and systemic activities.  \n- Both utilize chemical messengers (neurotransmitters in the nervous system, hormones in the endocrine system) for signal transmission.  \n- Both are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.  \n\n**Differences**:  \n- **Structure**: The nervous system consists of interconnected neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of discrete, unconnected glands.  \n- **Transmission**: The nervous system uses electrochemical pulses (nerve impulses) for rapid, direct signal transmission. The endocrine system relies on hormones released into the circulatory system, resulting in slower, widespread signal distribution.  \n- **Physical Connectivity**: Nervous system cells are physically interconnected, whereas endocrine organs operate independently without direct physical connections.  \n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 14.624, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 25199, 2663, 1321, 80583, 2663, 9730, 3844, 46699, 1321, 23892, 11074, 7938, 1046, 1032, 1267, 1438, 69656, 2754, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 6467, 7766, 54022, 1536, 110019, 1321, 39361, 16885, 1044, 9392, 1044, 3338, 1044, 1321, 27682, 9216, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 40013, 11883, 8871, 23740, 1319, 1546, 3317, 5207, 3674, 3701, 1294, 1278, 25199, 2663, 1044, 52832, 1294, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1041, 1394, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 1584, 30317, 1536, 8289, 17887, 12630, 1046, 1256, 1267, 1438, 1068, 13831, 3224, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 50947, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 15730, 1307, 78490, 45375, 3459, 1044, 3016, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1395, 16815, 1307, 33123, 1044, 1457, 31390, 65067, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 6881, 5061, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 8942, 60732, 43812, 1319, 2356, 1672, 118855, 1041, 1394, 8744, 1044, 3236, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1531, 80583, 2663, 48527, 1408, 52832, 7358, 2203, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 1044, 9903, 1294, 37625, 1044, 28759, 4987, 7507, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 85418, 26290, 3078, 5450, 87187, 1718, 2663, 3459, 1584, 33599, 78490, 1044, 11275, 80583, 31918, 21590, 22272, 3816, 3236, 8137, 20053, 1046, 1256, 1267, 62386, 1317, 4832, 4057, 1408, 4265, 42679, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.3645, -0.0491, -0.5336, -0.0776, -0.0173, -0.0513, 