{"id": "635", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the key similarities and differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters and hormones) to transmit signals.\n* Both systems have negative feedback mechanisms to regulate their function.\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of glands.\n* Transmission of signals occurs through electrical impulses in the nervous system, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n* The nervous system has a continuous structure, with cells connected to each other, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs not physically connected to each other.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to transmit signals.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The nervous system and endocrine system share key similarities and exhibit distinct differences. \n\n**Similarities**:  \n- Both systems maintain homeostasis by coordinating and regulating cellular, tissue, organ, and systemic activities.  \n- Both utilize chemical messengers (neurotransmitters in the nervous system, hormones in the endocrine system) for signal transmission.  \n- Both are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.  \n\n**Differences**:  \n- **Structure**: The nervous system consists of interconnected neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of discrete, unconnected glands.  \n- **Transmission**: The nervous system uses electrochemical pulses (nerve impulses) for rapid, direct signal transmission. The endocrine system relies on hormones released into the circulatory system, resulting in slower, widespread signal distribution.  \n- **Physical Connectivity**: Nervous system cells are physically interconnected, whereas endocrine organs operate independently without direct physical connections.  \n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 14.607, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 25199, 2663, 1321, 80583, 2663, 9730, 3844, 46699, 1321, 23892, 11074, 7938, 1046, 1032, 1267, 1438, 69656, 2754, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 6467, 7766, 54022, 1536, 110019, 1321, 39361, 16885, 1044, 9392, 1044, 3338, 1044, 1321, 27682, 9216, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 40013, 11883, 8871, 23740, 1319, 1546, 3317, 5207, 3674, 3701, 1294, 1278, 25199, 2663, 1044, 52832, 1294, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1041, 1394, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 12953, 1584, 30317, 1536, 8289, 17887, 12630, 1046, 1256, 1267, 1438, 1068, 13831, 3224, 5450, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 50947, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 15730, 1307, 78490, 45375, 3459, 1044, 3016, 1278, 80583, 2663, 1395, 16815, 1307, 33123, 1044, 1457, 31390, 65067, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 6881, 5061, 5450, 1531, 25199, 2663, 8942, 60732, 43812, 1319, 2356, 1672, 118855, 1041, 1394, 8744, 1044, 3236, 4987, 11724, 1046, 1531, 80583, 2663, 48527, 1408, 52832, 7358, 2203, 1278, 4087, 33012, 2663, 1044, 9903, 1294, 37625, 1044, 28759, 4987, 7507, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 1603, 85418, 26290, 3078, 5450, 87187, 1718, 2663, 3459, 1584, 33599, 78490, 1044, 11275, 80583, 31918, 21590, 22272, 3816, 3236, 8137, 20053, 1046, 125