{"id": "645", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "pred": "To plant a sprouted potato, first cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each, ensuring the long sprouts remain intact. Place the chunks on a tray in a cool, dark location overnight to dry the cut ends. Alternatively, small potatoes can be planted whole after being watered thoroughly. When planting, turn the soil to a depth of 12 inches, remove rocks and debris, and dig a 4-inch wide trench 6 to 8 inches deep. Space rows 24 to 36 inches apart if planting multiple rows. Place the potato chunks in the trench with the sprouted or eye side facing up, spacing each cube 6 to 8 inches apart. Cover with a layer of compost, then replace the dirt on top. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, keeping it 4 inches away from the sprouting vines to maintain soil coolness and moisture.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To plant a sprouted potato, first cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each, ensuring the long sprouts remain intact. Place the chunks on a tray in a cool, dark location overnight to dry the cut ends. Alternatively, small potatoes can be planted whole after being watered thoroughly. When planting, turn the soil to a depth of 12 inches, remove rocks and debris, and dig a 4-inch wide trench 6 to 8 inches deep. Space rows 24 to 36 inches apart if planting multiple rows. Place the potato chunks in the trench with the sprouted or eye side facing up, spacing each cube 6 to 8 inches apart. Cover with a layer of compost, then replace the dirt on top. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, keeping it 4 inches away from the sprouting vines to maintain soil coolness and moisture.", "time_sec": 14.025, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 7411, 1261, 75581, 7239, 68334, 1044, 2158, 6945, 1494, 2203, 63308, 1454, 2295, 1505, 3300, 5731, 2744, 1044, 40227, 1278, 2730, 75581, 14694, 10399, 28890, 1046, 22435, 1278, 63308, 1408, 1261, 40680, 1294, 1261, 12921, 1044, 8500, 7285, 32164, 1317, 12689, 1278, 6945, 15202, 1046, 37346, 1044, 3709, 73710, 1710, 1402, 54952, 6836, 2453, 3144, 4180, 1286, 43850, 1046, 4925, 78398, 1044, 3884, 1278, 14784, 1317, 1261, 12883, 1307, 1032, 1049, 1050, 29466, 1044, 8559, 34176, 1321, 50629, 1044, 1321, 5645, 1261, 1032, 1052, 44830, 9924, 79792, 1032, 1054, 1317, 1032, 1056, 29466, 8378, 1046, 20659, 12964, 1032, 1050, 1052, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1054, 29466, 13292, 1693, 78398, 6245, 12964, 1046, 22435, 1278, 68334, 63308, 1294, 1278, 79792, 1454, 1278, 75581, 7239, 1505, 12128, 4258, 22116, 2015, 1044, 37891, 2744, 50061, 1032, 1054, 1317, 1032, 1056, 29466, 13292, 1046, 31652, 1454, 1261, 6240, 1307, 62042, 1044, 2430, 14422, 1278, 47945, 1408, 3977, 1046, 6225, 1261, 1032, 1052, 44830, 6240, 1307, 15410, 1331, 3879, 1278, 12474, 1044, 18528, 1494, 1032, 1052, 29466, 5109, 1562, 1278, 75581, 26717, 1330, 2783, 1317, 7766, 14784, 12921, 3651, 1321, 39493, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1519, -0.0168, -0.6539, -0.0001, -0.0026, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0014, -0.0102, -0.6855, -0.3115, -0.1415, -