{"id": "648", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Normal urine is typically pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome. If kidney diseases are present, the filtration and re-absorption stages of urine production may be malfunctioning, altering this pale color. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods and medications can also affect urine color, with beets, berries, and fava beans being among the most likely to cause changes.", "pred": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "time_sec": 8.072, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": 