{"id": "649", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate different health conditions. Red urine may indicate the presence of blood and could be a sign of an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine can be a characteristic of porphyria, a rare disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.", "pred": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "time_sec": 8.003, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 4558, 1307, 35180, 1710, 10982, 5561, 4612, 5481, 1046, 98668, 4804, 35180, 12837, 4938, 2156, 1395, 6517, 1294, 1278, 35180, 1044, 1799, 2481, 1402, 1261, 2287, 1307, 