{"id": "651", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the color of urine can indicate various things, including:\n\n* Blood in the urine (passage 1)\n* Porphyria (a rare inherited disorder) (passage 2)\n* Kidney diseases (passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What does the color of urine mean?\" is:\n\nAnswer: Depending on the passage, the color of urine can indicate different things, such as blood, porphyria, or kidney diseases.", "pred": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "time_sec": 8.013, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 4558, 1307, 35180, 1710, 10982, 5561,