{"id": "652", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine can indicate various things. Here's what we can infer from the passages:\n\n* Red urine (passage 1) indicates the presence of blood in the urine, which can be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer.\n* Deep purple urine (passage 2) is associated with porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Certain foods and medications can also change urine color.\n* The normal color of urine is pale yellow (passage 3), but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is the meaning of different colors of urine?\" based on these passages is:\n\nRed urine can indicate the presence of blood in the urine, while deep purple urine is associated with porphyria. Changes in urine color can also be caused by kidney diseases.", "pred": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Seeing red urine typically means there is blood in the urine, which could be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. The normal color of urine is pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome, but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.", "time_sec": 8.027, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 1531, 4558, 1307, 35180, 1710, 10982, 5561, 4612, 5481, 1046, 98668, 4804, 35180, 12837, 4938, 2156, 1395, 6517, 1294, 1278, 35180, 1044, 1799, 2481, 1402, 1261, 2287, 1307, 4433, 11304, 2479, 1420, 10650, 1505, 6742, 1046, 34244, 47568, 35180, 1395, 1420, 25330, 17289, 1307, 2173, 21570, 4313, 1044, 1261, 11191, 1044, 40544, 18772, 1307, 4804, 6517, 3459, 1046, 1531, 5270, 4558, 1307, 35180, 1395, 28521, 19502, 1044, 3964, 1317, 1278, 42284, 90076, 48077, 1044, 1809, 1593, 4558, 1710, 1402, 24992, 1294, 5443, 1307, 25784, 14060, 2478, 1278, 50031, 1321, 27976, 1344, 1045, 110589, 15915, 1307, 35180, 5466, 1584, 122314, 1302, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0718, -0.0064, -0.3717, -0.0927, -0.0011, -0.0036, -0.2592, -0.08, -0.0784, -0.0842, -0.0007, -0.3286, -0.8441, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.1036, -0.7539, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0014, -0.7034, -0.7155, -0.1724, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.7194, -0.0, -0.1039, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.6114, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0537, -0.2738, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.297, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0093, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0236, -0.1446, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0548, -0.6714, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0035, -0.0, -0.1607, -0.0339, -0.0072, -0.5859, -0.014, -0.0139, -0.0001, -0.0074, -0.0014, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0072, -0.5669, -0.0537, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0023, -0.0002, -0.0035, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0086, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.2271], "cumulative_logprob": -9.3526, "norm_logp": -0.0891, "input_len": 310, "output_tokens": 105, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "653", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "To properly clean your hair, first select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. Ensure your water is warm but not too hot, and thoroughly wet your hair. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through the hair. If your hair is long, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles rather than piling it on your head. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove any tangles. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and let it stay on for a few minutes. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Pat dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoid rubbing it with the towel as it can cause damage. For complete drying, a hair dryer can be used.", "pred": "To properly clean your hair, first select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. Wet your hair with warm (not too hot) water in the shower, then apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo to your palm and work it through your hair, using your fingers to comb through longer hair and reduce tangles. Rinse the hair completely, and if it is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply conditioner in the same manner as shampoo, allow it to remain on for a few minutes, then rinse with cool water and comb through again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing back and forth or in circles to prevent damage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To properly clean your hair, first select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. Wet your hair with warm (not too hot) water in the shower, then apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo to your palm and work it through your hair, using your fingers to comb through longer hair and reduce tangles. Rinse the hair completely, and if it is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply conditioner in the same manner as shampoo, allow it to remain on for a few minutes, then rinse with cool water and comb through again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing back and forth or in circles to prevent damage.", "time_sec": 11.817, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 17103, 9375, 2143, 10188, 1044, 2158, 5762, 1278, 3875, 1627, 2372, 12078, 1321, 6570, 1258, 1394, 2143, 10188, 2658, 1046, 66195, 2143, 10188, 1454, 15701, 1319, 3715, 4382, 8480, 1041, 4180, 1294, 1278, 37809, 1044, 2430, 11145, 1261, 52718, 41720, 5647, 1307, 1627, 2372, 12078, 1317, 2143, 36631, 1321, 2196, 1494, 2645, 2143, 10188, 1044, 2505, 2143, 17296, 1317, 3830, 2645, 7934, 10188, 1321, 9980, 19953, 2013, 1046, 65117, 1415, 1278, 10188, 10185, 1044, 1321, 1693, 1494, 1395, 7934, 1044, 2210, 1261, 9924, 6793, 2279, 3830, 1317, 8559, 19953, 2013, 1321, 17208, 1278, 10188, 1046, 63882, 6570, 1258, 1294, 1278, 2879, 11665, 1435, 1627, 2372, 12078, 1044, 3894, 1494, 1317, 10399, 1408, 1394, 1261, 4517, 7334, 1044, 2430, 38124, 1415, 1454, 12921, 4180, 1321, 3830, 2645, 2790, 1046, 63322, 1278, 10188, 1454, 1261, 74537, 2505, 1261, 2350, 3333, 1505, 69956, 1302, 12968, 1044, 40052, 77487, 2595, 1321, 19888, 1505, 1294, 35438, 1317, 7495, 10605, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0802, -0.0106, -0.3271, -0.007, -0.0, -0.0026, -0.0, -0.0304, -0.1952, -0.2655, -0.1215, -0.6737, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0215, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.6177, -0.6337, -0.0899, -0.0, -0.12, -0.0008, -0.2752, -0.0102, -0.1712, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.8235, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.6163, -0.2762, -0.0115, -0.0013, -0.0023, -0.2231, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.