{"id": "662", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "pred": "Vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:  \n- Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water for a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and balance skin pH levels.  \n- Spray vinegar full-strength on the dog’s coat to normalize skin pH balance.  \n- Dilute apple cider vinegar with 50% water to soothe itchy ears using a cotton swab or gauze pad.  \n- Use vinegar in ear cleaning, flea repellent sprays, and flea baths (mixed with soap) to fight fleas.  \n- Rinse the dog after flea treatments.", "time_sec": 11.133, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 110382, 8374, 1710, 1402, 2434, 1394, 25007, 1294, 4631, 9384, 1058, 1256, 1010, 1045, 28978, 1032, 1049, 19339, 1307, 61359, 8374, 1454, 1032, 1050, 1045, 1052, 60180, 1307, 4180, 1394, 1261, 2778, 38124, 1415, 1317, 1344, 5517, 2154, 1419, 1278, 26100, 1321, 13864, 9877, 1274, 1072, 5283, 1046, 1256, 1010, 1045, 3434, 2291, 61359, 8374, 5275, 37086, 2750, 1408, 1278, 10575, 2