{"id": "697", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's instructions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. For a creamy and flavorful base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly before using it as a base for your desired ice cream flavor.", "pred": "To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, then heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract, chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, then heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract, chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "time_sec": 10.363, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 3180, 16254, 38423, 1044, 2158, 22903, 24224, 1044, 38423, 1044, 1321, 21842, 2203, 1261, 52812, 6318, 2136, 4253, 9374, 4570, 1278, 24224, 1934, 28862, 1044, 2430, 9374, 1278, 13810, 2586, 4570, 1494, 1395, 8480, 1321, 1261, 3709, 10749, 1307, 50842, 10249, 3879, 1278, 10314, 1046, 44250, 1278, 38423, 13810, 1317, 1261, 6212, 30831, 11024, 1321, 22903, 1294, 99927, 9041, 1044, 1528, 9184, 1278, 11986, 43850, 1394, 1513, 4403, 1032, 1050, 7700, 1046, 10108, 1278, 13074, 11986, 2203, 1420, 16254, 38423, 69947, 1044, 3884, 1408, 1278, 8832, 1044, 1321, 121978, 1394, 1032, 1050, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1053, 7334, 1046, 4925, 1278, 16254, 38423, 1395, 45118, 32362, 1044, 11584, 1494, 10912, 1505, 3535, 1261, 13079, 1307, 17985, 30711, 7655, 1408, 1278, 16254, 38423, 1321, 52659, 1317, 21033, 1262, 1394, 1032, 1050, 1317, 1032, 1051, 7700, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.1198, -0.0281, -0.514, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0006, -0.0113, -0.966, -0.8524, -0.0099, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0601, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0036, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0947, -0.132, -0.0, -0.6579, -0.0004, -0.6582, -0.6494, -0.0001, -0.4047, -0.2299, -0.2243, -0.0002, -0.2303, -0.1417, -0.0, -0.0558, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0235, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.5533, -0.1543, -0.0086, -0.0557, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.2155, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.5705, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.1875, -0.4793, -0.0, -0.643, -0.0158, -0.0017, -0.0373, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0204, -0.0, -0.0067, -0.0079, -0.4825, -0.2776, -0.164, -0.5136, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1165, -0.1145, -0.0939, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0027, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0661, -0.0337, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0014, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.217, -0.1035, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.2682, -0.2579, -0.0002, -0.0672, -0.4816, -0.4462, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0149, -0.0, -0.0911, -0.1362, -0.0, -0.0031, -0.9612, -0.7672, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0785, -1.2846], "cumulative_logprob": -16.0857, "norm_logp": -0.1149, "input_len": 358, "output_tokens": 140, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 81.29, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "698", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "pred": "To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, then heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract, chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ice cream, first stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, then heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract, chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Pour the cold mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and freeze to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "time_sec": 10.437, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 3180, 16254, 38423, 1044, 2158, 22903, 24224, 1044, 38423, 1044, 1321, 21842, 2203, 1261, 52812, 6318, 2136, 4253, 9374, 4570, 1278, 24224, 1934, 28862, 1044, 2430, 9374, 1278, 13810, 2586, 4570, 1494, 1395, 8480, 1321, 1261, 3709, 10749, 1307, 50842, 10249, 3879, 1278, 10314, 1046, 44250, 1278, 38423, 13810, 1317, 1261, 6212, 30831, 11024, 1321, 22903, 1294, 99927, 9041, 1044, 1528, 9184, 1278, 11986