{"id": "717", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, first, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod, then crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it remains upright and no water gets inside. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for about six minutes. After cooking, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Finally, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate. The PoachPod can be cleaned in a dishwasher.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "time_sec": 10.228, "nemotron":