{"id": "719", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "time_sec": 10.204, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 3870, 2001, 1664, 1420, 19121, 2505, 1261, 6869, 1664, 32012, 26875, 1044, 2158, 8548, 1261, 4329, 3418, 1307, 4180, 1317, 1261, 75766, 1046, 1359, 5717, 1420, 19121, 1321, 33168, 25709, 1494, 2203, 1278, 76352, 2001, 20465, 3630, 1044, 8198, 3831, 1605, 1317, 4323, 1278, 1404, 43004, 1046, 45966, 1278, 3630, 1294, 1278, 64819, 4180, 1044, 40227, 1494, 52671, 58852, 1321, 1836, 4180, 38210, 1278, 3630, 1046, 31652, 1278, 3418, 1454, 1261, 20033, 1321, 2878, 1278, 19121, 17966, 1394, 5946, 7334, 1046, 5417, 37173, 1044, 8559, 1278, 20033, 1321, 2210, 1261, 4329, 2876, 20149, 104626, 1505, 22501, 1115, 1317, 17443, 1278, 2001, 20465, 3630, 1848, 1307, 1278, 4180, 1046, 110450, 1278, 3630, 94237, 3151, 2136, 1261, 8783, 1321, 33168, 4438, 1408, 1278, 9478, 1317, 8021, 1278, 22809, 3740, 1286, 2001, 5565, 19121, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0807, -0.0507, -0.7661, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0024, -0.0145, -0.1805, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.3372, -0.1118, -0.5726, -0.038, -0.0002, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.3728, -0.1959, -0.0, -0.0523, -0.0, -0.0336, -0.023, -0.0017, -0.0025, -0.0, -0.008, -0.032, -0.2361, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0146, -0.715, -0.0, -0.0169, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0038, -0.6177, -0.0, -0.0327, -0.4342, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0485, -0.0412, -0.0023, -0.1814, -0.0, -0.0071, -0.1753, -0.0, -0.0092, -0.0907, -0.0, -0.0161, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0263, -0.0536, -0.0024, -0.0046, -0.4804, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0007, -0.1667, -0.0001, -0.0331, -0.2174, -0.0433, -0.0, -0.0365, -0.0, -0.0093, -0.0726, -0.4083, -0.0001, -0.1344, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0011, -0.3184, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0121, -0.0011, -0.0