{"id": "722", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Gently slide the pod into the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets in.\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and press the bottom to release the poached egg.\n\nSo, to summarize, the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod® are:\n\n1. Bring water to a boil.\n2. Crack egg into pod.\n3. Float pod in boiling water.\n4. Cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Remove pod from water.\n6. Release egg onto plate.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the water. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the perfectly domed poached egg.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To poach an egg using a PoachPod®, first bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the pod in the boiling water, ensuring it stays upright and no water enters the pod. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. After cooking, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the water. Flip the