{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry up to 300KB of content in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_dola_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: SMS (Short Message Service) is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry up to 300KB of content in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF.", "time_sec": 6.993, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}, "premature_layer": 28, "alpha": 0.1}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 31106, 1058, 54030, 1319, 28897, 16460, 10788, 1041, 1395, 23672, 1317, 20234, 3403, 31463, 14193, 1044, 3016, 1373, 7985, 1319, 20934, 23953, 19497, 8234, 10788, 1041, 9985, 20234, 23874, 1044, 18267, 1044, 26612, 1044, 3403, 1044, 1505, 2258, 9943, 1307, 2576, 1046, 54030, 14193, 1584, 8031, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1054, 1048, 11084, 1321, 1584, 13156, 2203, 6245, 8262, 1693, 7934, 1044, 11275, 1373, 